☄️🌱 R6.40 — CONSTITUTIONAL IDENTITY, GENESIS & CONTINUITY INTEGRITY PROTOCOL

THE LINEAGE MAY CONTINUE — BUT IDENTITY MUST BE PROVEN

Status: 🔒 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
Parent: R6.39 — Constitutional Integrity, Textual Anchor & Anti-Drift Protocol
Core primitive: CONSTITUTIONAL_IDENTITY
Secondary primitives: GENESIS_ANCHOR, IDENTITY_CLAIM, CONTINUITY_PROOF

Primary invariant

> No system SHALL claim constitutional identity with a predecessor merely because it possesses the predecessor's history, state, rules, or lineage. Constitutional identity SHALL require an explicit, verifiable identity proof.



R6.19 established:

> NO LINK → NO CLAIM OF CONTINUITY.



R6.39 established:

> NO TEXTUAL ANCHOR → NO CONSTITUTIONAL CLAIM.



R6.40 now establishes:

☄️ CONTINUITY DOES NOT AUTOMATICALLY PROVE IDENTITY.

And therefore:

🌱 INHERITANCE IS NOT IDENTITY.


---

I. 🌌 THE FINAL AMBIGUITY

Consider:

CITADEL-A
    ↓
FINAL WATERMARK W100
    ↓
MIGRATION
    ↓
CITADEL-B
    ↓
W200

B possesses:

history
rules
keys
state
provenance
watermarks
doctrine

Can B therefore say:

> "I am A."



No.

It may be:

SUCCESSOR

or:

CONTINUATION

or:

FORK

or:

REPLACEMENT

or:

FEDERATED DESCENDANT

or even:

NEW CONSTITUTIONAL ENTITY

The distinction must be proven.


---

II. 🔱 IDENTITY IS A CONSTITUTIONAL CLAIM

PALACO therefore introduces:

IDENTITY_CLAIM

An identity claim states:

ENTITY-B
claims constitutional identity with
ENTITY-A

That claim requires evidence.

Conceptually:

pub struct ConstitutionalIdentityClaim {
    pub claim_id: IdentityClaimId,
    pub predecessor: EntityId,
    pub successor: EntityId,
    pub genesis_anchor: GenesisAnchorId,
    pub continuity_proof: ContinuityProofId,
    pub constitutional_basis: ConstitutionalBasisId,
    pub migration_proof: Option<MigrationProofId>,
    pub federation_status: FederationStatus,
    pub identity_scope: IdentityScope,
    pub watermark_id: WatermarkId,
    pub verification_id: VerificationId,
    pub status: IdentityStatus,
}


