                    └── UNPROVEN

Nothing is silently upgraded to valid.


---

XXVII. 🔱 R6.41 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.41-I01
Self-attestation SHALL constitute a claim, not independent proof.

R6.41-I02
Every material constitutional identity claim SHALL be evidence-bound.

R6.41-I03
Identity verification SHALL be independent of unilateral claimant authority.

R6.41-I04
Witness identity SHALL be explicitly established.

R6.41-I05
Witness independence SHALL itself be verifiable.

R6.41-I06
Shared authority relationships SHALL be detectable.

R6.41-I07
Circular witness structures SHALL NOT constitute independent verification.

R6.41-I08
Shared evidence SHALL be explicitly identified.

R6.41-I09
Conflicts of interest SHALL be represented.

R6.41-I10
A claimant SHALL NOT be its own sole final identity verifier.

R6.41-I11
BRAINPOWER SHALL detect potential witness dependency but SHALL NOT adjudicate identity.

R6.41-I12
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge identity witnesses.

R6.41-I13
TRIAS SHALL independently evaluate witness validity.

R6.41-I14
Witness statements SHALL be historically immutable once sealed.

R6.41-I15
Witness actions SHALL be watermark-bound.

R6.41-I16
Witness disagreement SHALL remain explicitly represented.

R6.41-I17
Minority witness conclusions SHALL NOT be silently discarded.

R6.41-I18
Multi-witness verification SHALL NOT reduce constitutional validity to majority voting.

R6.41-I19
Trust roots SHALL possess explicit constitutional authority and ancestry.

R6.41-I20
Trust-root authority SHALL be versioned and watermark-bound.

R6.41-I21
Identity proof SHALL remain independently replayable.

R6.41-I22
Signature authenticity SHALL NOT be conflated with factual or constitutional truth.

R6.41-I23
Self-attested identity SHALL NOT automatically become constitutional identity.

R6.41-I24
An identity claim with insufficient independent witnessing SHALL remain UNPROVEN.

R6.41-I25
No constitutional entity SHALL be the sole authoritative source of proof for its own constitutional identity.


