XXX. 🔱 R6.42 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.42-I01
A constitutional proof SHALL remain historically addressable after witness retirement.

R6.42-I02
Witness retirement SHALL NOT erase historical attestations.

R6.42-I03
Witness succession SHALL be explicitly recorded.

R6.42-I04
Witness succession SHALL NOT retroactively transfer prior attestations.

R6.42-I05
Historical witness authority SHALL be evaluated according to its temporal validity.

R6.42-I06
Current witness invalidity SHALL NOT automatically invalidate historically valid attestations.

R6.42-I07
Witness revocation SHALL possess provenance and temporal scope.

R6.42-I08
Witness compromise SHALL be represented as an event rather than silent historical deletion.

R6.42-I09
Cryptographic key compromise SHALL NOT erase original evidence.

R6.42-I10
Historical signatures SHALL remain distinguishable from later preservation attestations.

R6.42-I11
Cryptographic re-anchoring SHALL NOT rewrite historical authorship.

R6.42-I12
Archived witnesses SHALL remain independently addressable.

R6.42-I13
A successor witness SHALL NOT impersonate the historical predecessor.

R6.42-I14
BRAINPOWER SHALL detect witness gaps and anomalies but SHALL NOT fabricate successors.

R6.42-I15
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge witness succession and historical validity.

R6.42-I16
TRIAS SHALL independently verify witness authority at the relevant historical time.

R6.42-I17
Witness disappearance SHALL NOT automatically imply proof invalidity.

R6.42-I18
Missing historical witness evidence SHALL remain explicitly represented.

R6.42-I19
Secondary evidence SHALL NOT silently become primary witness testimony.

R6.42-I20
Independent archival custody SHALL remain distinct from original witnessing.

R6.42-I21
Historical witness records SHALL remain replayable where sufficient evidence survives.

R6.42-I22
Epistemic redundancy SHALL preserve multiple independent verification paths.

R6.42-I23
Witness disagreement SHALL remain historically preserved.

R6.42-I24
Proof recovery SHALL require explicit evidence and independent review.

R6.42-I25
No missing witness SHALL ever be synthetically invented to restore continuity.


