XXXII. ☄️ THE BIG PRINCIPLE

R6.42 makes this canonical:

> The validity of a historical constitutional proof SHALL NOT depend solely upon the continued existence, availability, or current authority of its original witness.



Or:

WITNESS MAY DIE.

AUTHORITY MAY ROTATE.

KEYS MAY RETIRE.

SYSTEMS MAY EVOLVE.

CITADELS MAY MIGRATE.

BUT PROVEN HISTORY MUST REMAIN PROVABLE.


