The verifier compares:

StateRoot
EventRoot
RuleSetHash
ProvenanceRoot
Timestamp
Predecessor
Signature

Conceptually:

Compare(WA, WB)
      ↓
MATCH
PARTIAL_MATCH
CONFLICT
UNCOMPARABLE

UNCOMPARABLE is important.

Different domains may simply not possess enough shared information to establish equivalence.


---

VII. 🔬 WATERMARK EQUIVALENCE

Two watermarks may be considered equivalent only when the required commitments match under the declared equivalence rules.

Not:

same timestamp

Not:

same state description

Not:

same human interpretation

But through cryptographically verifiable commitments.

Therefore:

SIMILARITY IS NOT EQUIVALENCE.


---

VIII. 🌳 HISTORICAL FORK

Sometimes the correct result is a genuine fork:

W10
                  │
             ┌────┴────┐
             ▼         ▼
            W11-A     W11-B

This does not necessarily indicate fraud.

It may represent:

parallel execution
jurisdictional divergence
network partition
legitimate constitutional branching

The fork becomes part of history.

It must not be silently collapsed.


---

IX. 💀 FORK ≠ DUPLICATION

A fork means:

one predecessor
multiple legitimate successors

A duplicate may mean:

same intended state
multiple conflicting identifiers

These are different conditions.

PALACO must distinguish:

FORK
DUPLICATION
REPLAY_DIVERGENCE
FABRICATION


---

X. 🔥 HISTORICAL RECONCILIATION

When archives disagree:

ARCHIVE A
ARCHIVE B
ARCHIVE C
    │
    ▼
RECONCILIATION ENGINE

The engine evaluates:

1. Provenance
2. Authority
3. Temporal ordering
4. Witness independence
5. Cryptographic integrity
6. Scope
7. Replayability
8. Lineage
9. Evidence quality
10. Known gaps

It produces a result.

Not a preference.


