E1 → E2 → E3

Archive B:
E1 → E3 → E2

The timestamps may be identical or near-identical.

R6.19 already established:

> CLOCK TIME ≠ CONSTITUTIONAL ORDER



R6.48 now adds:

> ARCHIVAL ORDER ≠ PROVEN ORDER



Order must be established through deterministic sequencing evidence.


---

XIX. 🧬 CAUSAL ORDER

Where constitutional dependencies exist:

E1 authorizes E2

then E2 cannot logically precede E1 merely because its timestamp is earlier.

The verifier examines:

predecessor references
sequence identifiers
dependency edges
authority references
event causality

This creates:

CONSTITUTIONAL ORDER

as distinct from wall-clock time.


---

XX. 💧 STATE ROOT DISPUTE

Suppose:

A-W10.StateRoot = X
B-W10.StateRoot = Y

The system cannot resolve this by declaring:

X = correct

It performs:

Replay(A-history)
Replay(B-history)

and asks:

Which state follows from the independently verified event/rule history?

Possible result:

A replay = X
B replay = Y

Then:

HISTORICAL_FORK

may be the correct conclusion.


