TRIAS verifies that closure was legitimate:

Question identity
Scope
Evidence
Provenance
Witness independence
Reconciliation
Threshold
Residual uncertainty
Challenge handling
Closure authority
Watermark

TRIAS may return:

CLOSURE_VALID

or:

CLOSURE_DEFECTIVE


---

XV. 🔐 CLOSURE WATERMARK

A closure receives its own watermark:

Q42
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
RECONCILIATION
 ↓
CLOSURE
 ↓
W-Q42-CLOSED

The closure becomes part of constitutional history.

It can therefore be replayed.


---

XVI. 🕰️ CLOSURE HAS TIME

The system must distinguish:

QUESTION_OPEN_AT T1
QUESTION_CLOSED_AT T2
QUESTION_REOPENED_AT T3

It must never rewrite:

T2

because reopening happened at:

T3

The historical record becomes:

OPEN
 ↓
CLOSED
 ↓
REOPENED

not:

OPEN
 ↓
"NEVER CLOSED"


---

XVII. 💧 CLOSURE DOES NOT ERASE UNCERTAINTY

A closure record must retain:

residual_uncertainty
known_gaps
excluded_domains
assumptions
confidence

For example:

CONCLUSION:
PROVEN

RESIDUAL:
E42's external diplomatic consequences unknown.

SCOPE:
constitutional authorization only.

This prevents epistemic inflation.


---

XVIII. 🔥 PROOF FINALITY LEVELS

PALACO may distinguish:

PROVISIONAL
SUPPORTED
PROVEN
FINALLY_PROVEN
GOVERNANCE_CLOSED

GOVERNANCE_CLOSED means:

> the constitutional process has reached the required stopping point for action.



It does not mean:

> the proposition can never be revisited.




---

XIX. 🌐 REOPENING THE THRESHOLD

A closed question may reopen when:

Materiality >= threshold
AND
Evidence authenticity = PASS
AND
Provenance = PASS
AND
Potential conclusion impact = significant

Conceptually:

NewEvidence
     ↓
MaterialityAssessment
     ↓
Threshold
     ↓
┌───────────────┐
│               │
PASS           FAIL
│               │
▼               ▼
REOPEN       PRESERVE

Failed reopening requests are themselves historical records.


---

XX. 🚫 NO INFINITE APPEAL LOOP

A failed reopening request must not automatically generate another reopening request indefinitely.

Therefore PALACO introduces:

REOPENING_COOLDOWN

and:

REOPENING_BASIS

A subsequent request must identify materially new grounds.

Otherwise:

same evidence
+
same argument
=
no new reopening basis


---

XXI. ⚓ QUAY

The Quay stores the complete closure lifecycle:

QUESTION
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
CHALLENGE
 ↓
REVIEW
 ↓
CLOSURE
 ↓
NEW EVIDENCE
 ↓
REOPENING
 ↓
REVIEW
 ↓
NEW CLOSURE

Nothing is deleted.

Nothing is retroactively rewritten.


---

XXII. 🌳 THE CLOSURE TREE

QUESTION Q42
                              │
                         EVIDENCE SET
                              │
                         RECONCILIATION
                              │
                         CLOSURE C1
                              │
                    ┌─────────┴─────────┐
                    │                   │
              RESIDUAL UNKNOWN     NEW EVIDENCE
                                        │
                                  REOPENING TEST
                                        │
                                  THRESHOLD PASS
                                        │
                                    CLOSURE C2

The second closure does not invalidate the fact that C1 existed.

It supersedes its operative conclusion.


