XXX. 🔬 CLOSURE AND TRIAS

TRIAS verifies:

Was the question properly defined?

Was the scope explicit?

Was the evidence sufficient?

Was contradictory evidence considered?

Was FOOL given challenge opportunity?

Was the reopening threshold predetermined?

Was residual uncertainty preserved?

Was the closure watermarked?

Can an independent verifier replay the conclusion?

Only then:

CLOSURE = VALID


---

XXXI. ☄️ THE EPISTEMIC CLOSURE EQUATION

Conceptually:

C = Close(
    Q,
    E,
    P,
    W,
    R,
    U,
    T
)

where:

Q = Question
E = Evidence
P = Provenance
W = Witnesses
R = Reconciliation
U = Residual Uncertainty
T = Closure Threshold

And reopening:

O = Reopen(
    C,
    E_new,
    P_new,
    M_new,
    T
)

where:

M_new = MaterialityAssessment

Thus:

CLOSED
  +
MATERIAL NEW EVIDENCE
  +
VALID PROVENANCE
  +
THRESHOLD PASS
  =
REOPENED


---

XXXII. 🔥 R6.49 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.49-I01
Constitutional questions SHALL possess explicit identities and scopes.

R6.49-I02
Epistemic closure SHALL NOT be equated with absolute certainty.

R6.49-I03
Closure SHALL require an explicit evidentiary and procedural basis.

R6.49-I04
Closure scope SHALL be explicitly declared.

R6.49-I05
A closed question SHALL NOT automatically close related questions.

R6.49-I06
Residual uncertainty SHALL remain preserved after closure.

R6.49-I07
Closure SHALL itself possess provenance.

R6.49-I08
Closure SHALL be represented by an immutable historical record once sealed.

R6.49-I09
Material new evidence SHALL remain capable of triggering reopening.

R6.49-I10
Reopening SHALL require satisfaction of an explicit threshold.

R6.49-I11
Evidence already considered SHALL NOT automatically qualify as new evidence.

R6.49-I12
Reopening requests SHALL themselves become auditable historical records.

R6.49-I13
A failed reopening request SHALL NOT erase the underlying challenge.

R6.49-I14
BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT autonomously convert discovery into reopening authority.

R6.49-I15
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge epistemic closure.

R6.49-I16
TRIAS SHALL verify closure methodology and threshold compliance.

R6.49-I17
Correction SHALL remain distinct from reopening.

R6.49-I18
Reopening SHALL NOT rewrite the historical fact that an earlier closure occurred.

R6.49-I19
Federated closure SHALL remain scoped to the federation's declared jurisdiction.

R6.49-I20
Local closure SHALL NOT automatically establish planetary closure.

R6.49-I21
Closure authority SHALL itself be constitutionally bounded.

R6.49-I22
Repeated identical claims SHALL NOT create infinite reopening cycles.

R6.49-I23
A closure without sufficient evidence SHALL be invalid.

R6.49-I24
A new closure SHALL supersede prior operative conclusions without erasing their historical existence.

R6.49-I25
Where evidence remains insufficient, PALACO SHALL preserve uncertainty rather than manufacture finality.


