      ↓
W-B-GENESIS


---

XXI. 🕰️ NO RETROACTIVE AUTHORITY

Unless explicitly and constitutionally permitted, B must not claim:

B authority existed before B existed.

Therefore:

EffectiveAt(B) > Genesis(B)

and historical actions are evaluated according to the authority applicable at their own constitutional time.

This becomes:

AUTHORITY IS TEMPORAL.


---

XXII. 🧬 SUCCESSION AND R6.49

R6.49 established that closure is scoped.

R6.50 applies that principle to constitutional generations.

A successor may say:

A's historical question Q42 was closed.

It may not automatically say:

Q42 is permanently immune from all future constitutional review.

The reopening rules of the successor must explicitly govern the question.

Thus:

A-Closure
   ↓
B-Inheritance
   ↓
B-ReopeningPolicy

The closure survives historically.

Its operative legal status may change.


---

XXIII. 💧 HISTORICAL MEMORY ≠ OPERATIVE STATE

This distinction is now canonical:

HISTORICAL MEMORY
        │
        ├── immutable
        ├── replayable
        └── provenance-bound

OPERATIVE CONSTITUTION
        │
        ├── current
        ├── mutable through lawful transition
        └── authority-bound

A successor changes the second.

It does not rewrite the first.


---

XXIV. ☄️ GENERATIONAL REPLAY

An independent verifier must be able to perform:

Replay(A-history)
       ↓
A-final-watermark

Verify(Succession)
       ↓
B-genesis-watermark

Replay(B-history)
       ↓
B-current-watermark

Thus:

A-history
   +
succession-proof
   +
B-history

forms a reproducible generational chain.


---

XXV. 🚨 SUCCESSION DIVERGENCE

If:

A-final = WA

but B claims:

predecessor = WX

then:

SUCCESSION_DIVERGENCE

The successor cannot become fully active on that lineage until the discrepancy is resolved or explicitly represented as a fork.


