XXVII. 🌌 GENESIS EPISTEMICS

R6.49 established:

> Closure is not certainty.



R6.51 applies the same principle to origins.

The system may establish:

GENESIS PROVEN

without claiming:

WE KNOW EVERYTHING THAT EXISTED BEFORE THIS.

This matters enormously.

A genesis boundary means:

> No earlier constitutional predecessor has been established under the applicable proof rules.



It does not mean:

> Nothing existed before this in any sense whatsoever.




---

XXVIII. 🧠 THE GENESIS EPISTEMIC BOUNDARY

Therefore PALACO records:

KNOWN:
Genesis begins here.

UNKNOWN:
Any pre-genesis conditions outside the declared constitutional scope.

PROVEN:
The foundation evidence supporting this genesis.

UNPROVEN:
Any claimed predecessor not supported by evidence.

This is precise epistemology.


