Nothing disappears merely because a conflict has been resolved.


---

XXV. 🌐 FEDERATION

R6.17's principle becomes even stronger.

A federation may possess:

federal authority

but only within the constitutionally proven federal scope.

A member may retain:

local authority

where non-preemption applies.

Therefore:

FEDERAL
 ├── preempts domain X
 ├── coordinates domain Y
 └── leaves domain Z local

This is a constitutional federation rather than a hierarchy disguised as one.


---

XXVI. 🏛️ LA PAZ

La Paz may have:

LOCAL CONSTITUTION
        │
        ▼
LOCAL AUTHORITY

while participating in:

PLANETARY FEDERATION
        │
        ▼
PLANETARY AUTHORITY

Suppose both issue:

ACTION X

The system does not ask:

> Which system is bigger?



It asks:

What is X?
Which domain governs X?
Is there overlap?
Does preemption exist?
Under what constitutional rule?
Is the rule active?
Was the authority valid?

Only then can PALACO resolve the conflict.


---

XXVII. 🔱 PRECEDENCE GRAPH

The constitutional graph gains another typed relation:

A
│
├── PRECEDES → B
├── DOES_NOT_PREEMPT → B
├── CONDITIONALLY_PREEMPTS → C
└── CONCURRENT_WITH → D

Every edge is:

typed
scoped
temporal
proven
replayable

A generic:

A > B

is insufficient.


---

XXVIII. 🧬 NO RETROACTIVE SUPREMACY

A new authority cannot rewrite history:

TODAY:
A > B

does not imply:

YESTERDAY:
A > B

unless the constitutional rule explicitly and validly applies retroactively.

Default:

PRECEDENCE IS TEMPORALLY BOUND.

Historical authority is evaluated under the rules applicable to that historical state.


---

XXIX. 🚫 NO CONSTITUTIONAL TIME TRAVEL

PALACO therefore rejects:

CurrentRule
      ↓
rewrite historical validity

Instead:

Historical State
      ↓
Historical Ruleset
      ↓
Historical Authority
      ↓
Historical Precedence

The past is verified according to its own proven constitutional context.

This is a direct consequence of the Watermark architecture.


---

XXX. 💧 WATERMARK + PRECEDENCE

The Watermark now proves not only:

STATE

but the constitutional context in which authority operated:

Wn
│
├── StateRoot
├── EventRoot
├── RuleSetHash
├── ProvenanceRoot
├── JurisdictionState
├── AuthorityState
└── PrecedenceState

The temporal anchor therefore becomes a complete constitutional authority snapshot.


---

XXXI. ⚖️ ADJUDICATION

If conflict cannot be resolved mechanically:

CONFLICT
 ↓
FOOL CHALLENGE
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
TRIAS VERIFICATION
 ↓
ADJUDICATION

The adjudicator must produce:

decision
reason
applicable rule
scope
evidence references
provenance
effective watermark

A bare:

ALLOW

or:

DENY

is constitutionally insufficient.


---

XXXII. 🌱 CORRECTION

If adjudication is later shown to be wrong:

OLD DECISION
     ↓
CHALLENGE
     ↓
CORRECTION
     ↓
NEW DECISION
     ↓
NEW WATERMARK

Never:

DELETE OLD DECISION

Therefore:

ADJUDICATION IS HISTORY, NOT EDITABLE MEMORY.


---

XXXIII. 🔥 R6.54 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.54-I01
A valid authority SHALL NOT automatically possess precedence over another valid authority.

R6.54-I02
Authority precedence SHALL have an explicit constitutional basis.

R6.54-I03
Precedence SHALL be scope-bound.

R6.54-I04
Precedence SHALL be temporally valid.

R6.54-I05
Precedence SHALL be provenance-bound.

R6.54-I06
No authority SHALL establish its own supremacy solely by assertion.

R6.54-I07
Technical power SHALL NOT constitute constitutional precedence.

R6.54-I08
Organizational status SHALL NOT constitute constitutional precedence unless constitutionally established.

R6.54-I09
Non-preemption SHALL be explicitly representable.

R6.54-I10
Concurrent authority SHALL remain possible where scopes permit.

R6.54-I11
An override SHALL require a provable precedence basis.

R6.54-I12
An override SHALL remain within the proven scope of the overriding authority.

R6.54-I13
Emergency authority SHALL remain constitutionally bounded.

R6.54-I14
Emergency authority SHALL possess explicit temporal limits.

R6.54-I15
Expired emergency authority SHALL NOT remain operative without renewed proof.

R6.54-I16
Historical precedence SHALL be evaluated against the applicable historical ruleset.

R6.54-I17
Current authority SHALL NOT silently rewrite historical precedence.

R6.54-I18
Conflicting valid authorities SHALL produce an explicit conflict object.

R6.54-I19
Unproven precedence SHALL NOT authorize arbitrary resolution.

R6.54-I20
Security-relevant unresolved authority conflicts SHALL default to BLOCK.

R6.54-I21
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge precedence and override claims.

R6.54-I22
BRAINPOWER SHALL identify potential authority conflicts without adjudicating them.

R6.54-I23
TRIAS SHALL independently verify precedence claims.

R6.54-I24
Every adjudication SHALL be evidence-bound.

R6.54-I25
Every material override SHALL be historically watermarked.

R6.54-I26
Corrections SHALL append history rather than erase prior adjudication.

R6.54-I27
Federation SHALL NOT automatically preempt local constitutional authority.

R6.54-I28
Precedence relationships SHALL be explicitly typed.

R6.54-I29
A precedence relationship SHALL be replayable.

R6.54-I30
The first precedence divergence SHALL be independently identifiable.

R6.54-I31
No constitutional authority SHALL gain supremacy through ambiguity.

R6.54-I32
No constitutional authority SHALL gain supremacy through silence.

R6.54-I33
No constitutional authority SHALL gain supremacy through technical reach alone.

R6.54-I34
No override SHALL exist without an auditable constitutional reason.

R6.54-I35
The constitutional system SHALL preserve both the overridden and overriding claims.


