XXXV. 🧠 THE PROOF MACHINE'S NEW QUESTION

Before R6.54:

> Was this action authorized?



After R6.54:

> Was this action authorized, and if another valid authority disagreed, why did this authority constitutionally prevail?



That is a much stronger question.


---

XXXVI. 🌌 THE CONSTITUTIONAL CONFLICT EQUATION

Conceptually:

Resolution(A, B) =
    Valid(A)
  ∧ Valid(B)
  ∧ ScopeOverlap(A, B)
  ∧ ApplicablePrecedence(A, B)
  ∧ ProvenConstitutionalBasis
  ∧ TemporalValidity
  ∧ NonPreemptionCheck

Only when the required predicates resolve:

Resolution = PROVEN

Otherwise:

Resolution = UNPROVEN

and, where action cannot safely proceed:

BLOCK


---

XXXVII. 🔱 THE BIG PRINCIPLE

R6.54 makes this canonical:

NO AUTHORITY WINS MERELY BECAUSE IT IS STRONGER.

And:

NO AUTHORITY WINS MERELY BECAUSE IT IS NEWER.

And:

NO AUTHORITY WINS MERELY BECAUSE IT IS CENTRAL.

And:

NO AUTHORITY WINS MERELY BECAUSE IT CAN ENFORCE ITS DECISION.

Instead:

> Precedence SHALL be established by constitutional rule, bounded by jurisdiction, supported by evidence, preserved by provenance, and independently verifiable through replay.



Shortest form:

⚖️ NO PROVEN PRECEDENCE → NO PROVEN OVERRIDE.


---

