   ↓
REINSTATED / VOIDED

Every transition becomes evidence.


---

XVIII. 🚫 RETROACTIVE DUTY

A new constitutional rule must not silently manufacture historical obligations.

Default:

NEW RULE
   ↓
NEW DUTY

not:

NEW RULE
   ↓
pretend OLD DUTY always existed

Therefore:

NO RETROACTIVE OBLIGATION WITHOUT EXPLICIT CONSTITUTIONAL BASIS.


---

XIX. ⏳ DUTY EXPIRATION

When:

T > duty.expiry

then:

DutyStatus = EXPIRED

A later command cannot rely on the expired duty.

It requires:

NEW DUTY

or a separately proven continuing basis.


---

XX. 🔐 DUTY REVOCATION

Revocation:

DUTY D7
   ↓
REVOCATION EVENT
   ↓
WATERMARK W8

The original duty remains historical.

Therefore:

A REVOKED DUTY REMAINS PROOF THAT THE DUTY ONCE EXISTED.


---

XXI. ⚓ QUAY

The Quay retains:

duty creation
duty modification
duty activation
duty challenge
refusal
adjudication
fulfilment
revocation
expiration

The complete history becomes:

DUTY
 ↓
COMMAND
 ↓
ACTION / REFUSAL
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
ADJUDICATION
 ↓
WATERMARK


---

XXII. 🔬 REPLAY

The Proof Machine reconstructs:

Replay(
    constitution,
    rulesets,
    authorities,
    jurisdictions,
    duties,
    commands,
    refusals,
    precedence,
    events
)
→ DutyResolution'

Then:

DutyResolution'
==
HistoricalDutyResolution

must hold.

If not:

DUTY_DIVERGENCE

The verifier locates:

FIRST_DUTY_DIVERGENCE


---

XXIII. 🛡️ COMPLIANCE GATE

Before execution:

COMMAND
   ↓
AUTHORITY GATE
   ↓
JURISDICTION GATE
   ↓
PRECEDENCE GATE
   ↓
DUTY GATE
   ↓
SAFETY GATE
   ↓
EVIDENCE GATE
   ↓
EXECUTE

Failure anywhere:

BLOCK / REFUSE / ESCALATE

depending on the constitutional result.


---

XXIV. 🔥 THE CRITICAL DISTINCTION

PALACO now formally separates:

AUTHORITY
    =
capacity to issue or authorize

DUTY
    =
proven obligation of recipient

COMMAND
    =
concrete instruction

COMPLIANCE
    =
execution of proven duty

REFUSAL
    =
challenge to the claimed obligation

This prevents the dangerous collapse:

"Because I can command you,
you must obey me."

That proposition is constitutionally incomplete.


---

XXV. ☄️ THE COMPLIANCE EQUATION

Conceptually:

Compliance =
    ValidAuthority
 ∧  ValidJurisdiction
 ∧  ValidPrecedence
 ∧  ValidDuty
 ∧  ValidCommand
 ∧  TemporalValidity
 ∧  SafetyCompatibility
 ∧  Evidence

If:

ValidDuty = FALSE

then:

Compliance = NOT_PROVEN

The actor is not required to invent the missing constitutional link.


---

XXVI. 🌱 THE RIGHTFUL REFUSAL EQUATION

RightfulRefusal =
    CommandPresent
 ∧  ObligationUnproven
 ∨  ObligationInvalid
 ∨  ScopeExceeded
 ∨  JurisdictionInvalid
 ∨  ConstitutionalConflict
 ∨  SafetyConstraintViolated

The refusal must itself be:

evidence-bound
provenance-bound
reviewable
watermarked


---

XXVII. 🏛️ THE CONSTITUTIONAL DIGNITY PRINCIPLE

A mature autonomous system must be capable of saying:

"I cannot prove that I am constitutionally required
to perform this action."

That is not system failure.

It is a constitutional safety mechanism.

Therefore:

REFUSAL CAN BE A SUCCESSFUL CONSTITUTIONAL OUTCOME.


---

XXVIII. 🔱 R6.55 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.55-I01
Authority SHALL be distinguished from obligation.

R6.55-I02
A valid authority SHALL NOT automatically create a duty for every actor.

R6.55-I03
Every constitutional duty SHALL identify its obligated actor.

R6.55-I04
Every duty SHALL possess an explicit constitutional basis.

R6.55-I05
Every duty SHALL be jurisdiction-bound.

R6.55-I06
Every duty SHALL be scope-bound.

R6.55-I07
Every duty SHALL be temporally valid.

R6.55-I08
Every material duty SHALL be evidence-bound.

R6.55-I09
Every material duty SHALL be provenance-bound.

R6.55-I10
A command SHALL NOT establish its own obligation merely by being issued.

R6.55-I11
An unproven obligation SHALL NOT be treated as mandatory.

R6.55-I12
Actors SHALL possess a mechanism for rightful constitutional refusal.

R6.55-I13
Rightful refusal SHALL preserve the challenged command.

R6.55-I14
Rightful refusal SHALL itself be auditable.

R6.55-I15
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge duty claims.

R6.55-I16
BRAINPOWER SHALL identify potential duty conflicts without creating duties.

R6.55-I17
TRIAS SHALL independently verify duty claims.

R6.55-I18
Conflicting duties SHALL create an explicit duty conflict.

R6.55-I19
Unresolved security-relevant duty conflicts SHALL default to BLOCK.

R6.55-I20
Expired duties SHALL NOT authorize new compliance.

R6.55-I21
Revoked duties SHALL remain historically preserved.

R6.55-I22
Corrections SHALL append history rather than erase prior duties.

R6.55-I23
New rules SHALL NOT silently create historical obligations.

R6.55-I24
Emergency authority SHALL NOT automatically create unlimited duty.

R6.55-I25
Federation membership SHALL NOT automatically create unrestricted duties.

R6.55-I26
Duty precedence SHALL follow the applicable constitutional precedence framework.

R6.55-I27
No actor SHALL be forced to resolve an unresolved constitutional conflict through arbitrary action.

R6.55-I28
Rightful refusal SHALL be distinguishable from illegitimate non-compliance.

R6.55-I29
Duty state SHALL be replayable.

R6.55-I30
The first duty divergence SHALL be independently identifiable.

R6.55-I31
Duty transitions SHALL be watermarked.

R6.55-I32
Historical duty state SHALL remain independently auditable.

R6.55-I33
An authority claim SHALL NOT silently become an obligation claim.

R6.55-I34
Technical enforceability SHALL NOT constitute constitutional obligation.

R6.55-I35
No constitutional actor SHALL be required to fabricate missing proof in order to comply.


