XXXII. 🔥 R6.56 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.56-I01
Authorization SHALL NOT be considered permanently valid merely because it passed pre-execution validation.

R6.56-I02
Live authorization SHALL remain bounded by its constitutional scope.

R6.56-I03
Long-running or high-risk actions SHALL support constitutional revalidation.

R6.56-I04
Revocation SHALL be capable of invalidating an in-flight authorization.

R6.56-I05
A stale authorization SHALL NOT be treated as live authorization.

R6.56-I06
Material constitutional state changes SHALL be capable of triggering revalidation.

R6.56-I07
Ruleset changes SHALL NOT be silently ignored during active execution.

R6.56-I08
Jurisdiction changes SHALL NOT be silently ignored during active execution.

R6.56-I09
Duty expiration SHALL invalidate dependent execution where applicable.

R6.56-I10
Revalidation SHALL be evidence-bound.

R6.56-I11
Revalidation SHALL be provenance-bound.

R6.56-I12
Revalidation SHALL identify the applicable Watermark.

R6.56-I13
A failed revalidation SHALL produce a defined constitutional interruption state.

R6.56-I14
Unknown live authority SHALL NOT be treated as valid authority.

R6.56-I15
Suspended actions SHALL require revalidation before resumption.

R6.56-I16
Resumption SHALL constitute a new constitutional checkpoint.

R6.56-I17
Final commit SHALL be subject to live constitutional validity where required.

R6.56-I18
Mid-action revocation SHALL remain historically auditable.

R6.56-I19
Constitutional abort SHALL preserve the action's historical evidence.

R6.56-I20
BRAINPOWER SHALL detect potential live-validity anomalies without granting authority.

R6.56-I21
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge live authorization.

R6.56-I22
TRIAS SHALL independently verify live validity.

R6.56-I23
Live authorization transitions SHALL be recorded in the Quay.

R6.56-I24
Material live authorization transitions SHALL be watermarked.

R6.56-I25
Live execution SHALL be deterministically replayable.

R6.56-I26
The first live-validity divergence SHALL be independently identifiable.

R6.56-I27
Cross-domain authorization SHALL remain valid only while its delegation remains valid.

R6.56-I28
Emergency authorization SHALL remain temporally bounded.

R6.56-I29
Emergency authority SHALL remain subject to live constitutional controls.

R6.56-I30
No actor SHALL continue an action solely because the action was valid at an earlier time.

R6.56-I31
No system SHALL silently convert authorization staleness into authorization validity.

R6.56-I32
A constitutional interruption SHALL itself be an auditable event.

R6.56-I33
A safe stop SHALL preserve enough state for independent forensic reconstruction.

R6.56-I34
No constitutional action SHALL bypass mandatory live revalidation.

R6.56-I35
Continuous constitutional validity SHALL be demonstrable through replay.


