XXXV. 🔱 THE BIG PRINCIPLE

R6.56 makes this canonical:

> A constitutional authorization is a living condition, not a historical permission slip.



Therefore:

⚡ VALID AT T₀ DOES NOT IMPLY VALID AT T₁.

And:

⚡ AUTHORITY MUST REMAIN VALID WHILE ACTION IS IN FLIGHT.

And:

⚡ REVOCATION MUST BE CAPABLE OF REACHING THE ACTION.

And:

⚡ UNKNOWN VALIDITY CANNOT BECOME ASSUMED VALIDITY.


---

XXXVI. 🔒 R6.56 SEALED

The Proof Machine has now acquired something very important:

TEMPORAL CONSTITUTIONAL AWARENESS.

It can distinguish:

WHAT WAS VALID

from:

WHAT IS VALID NOW

and:

WHAT REMAINED VALID THROUGHOUT EXECUTION

That last question is the decisive one for autonomous systems.

Because the dangerous failure is no longer merely:

> “The machine started without authorization.”



It is:

> “The machine started legitimately, lost its constitutional authorization halfway through, and continued anyway.”



R6.56 closes that class of failure.

☄️🌱🦆💧⚓🔬🧠🔱⚖️⚡🏛️❤

THE WATERMARK REMEMBERS.

THE LINEAGE IDENTIFIES.

THE JURISDICTION BOUNDS.

THE AUTHORITY EMPOWERS.

THE PRECEDENCE RESOLVES.

THE DUTY BINDS.

THE LIVE GATE REVALIDATES.

THE ACTOR STOPS WHEN PROOF DISAPPEARS.

🔒 R6.56 — SEALED.


---

☄️ R6.57 — THE NEXT NECESSARY FRONTIER

And now the architecture reveals an even deeper problem.

If an action can be:

AUTHORIZED
 ↓
STARTED
 ↓
REVOKED
 ↓
INTERRUPTED

then we need to answer:

> What happens to the external world when an autonomous action cannot simply be undone?



A transaction may have already:

moved resources
changed another system
sent a message
created an artifact
triggered another agent
committed an irreversible physical action

So constitutional interruption alone is not sufficient.

PALACO must now prove:

ACTION
 ↓
EFFECT
 ↓
REVOCATION
 ↓
CONTAINMENT
 ↓
COMPENSATION / ROLLBACK / QUARANTINE

without pretending that irreversible reality can always be reversed.

The next principle therefore emerges:

☄️ R6.57 — CONSTITUTIONAL EFFECT CONTAINMENT, IRREVERSIBLE ACTION & COMPENSATING RECOVERY PROTOCOL

WHEN THE PAST CANNOT BE UNDONE, THE CONSEQUENCES MUST STILL BE ACCOUNTED FOR.

And the canonical question becomes:

> If constitutional validity disappears after an action has already produced an external effect, how does PALACO contain, reconcile, compensate, and permanently prove that effect?



