Parent: R6.56 — Continuous Constitutional Validity, Live Authority Revalidation & Mid-Action Revocation
Core primitive: CONSTITUTIONAL_EFFECT
Secondary primitives: EFFECT_CONTAINMENT, IRREVERSIBLE_EFFECT, COMPENSATING_RECOVERY, EFFECT_RECONCILIATION

Primary invariant

> Every material external effect produced by a constitutional action SHALL remain attributable, observable, evidence-bound, provenance-bound, and recoverable or explicitly classified as irreversible.



R6.56 established:

> AUTHORITY MUST REMAIN VALID WHILE ACTION IS IN FLIGHT.



R6.57 confronts what happens when validity disappears after reality has already changed.

⚓ AN ACTION MAY STOP. ITS EFFECT MAY ALREADY EXIST.


---

I. 🌌 THE IRREVERSIBILITY PROBLEM

Consider:

T₀
AUTHORITY ✓
      ↓
ACTION
      ↓
EXTERNAL EFFECT
      ↓
T₁
AUTHORITY REVOKED

The system cannot honestly claim:

"Nothing happened."

Nor may it claim:

"The action was later revoked,
therefore the effect never existed."

That would destroy historical truth.

Instead:

EFFECT OCCURRED
      ↓
EFFECT ATTRIBUTED
      ↓
EFFECT CLASSIFIED
      ↓
CONTAINMENT
      ↓
RECOVERY / COMPENSATION / ACCEPTANCE
      ↓
PROOF


---

II. 🔱 EFFECT AS A FIRST-CLASS OBJECT

A material consequence becomes a constitutional object:

pub struct ConstitutionalEffect {
    pub effect_id: EffectId,
    pub action_id: ActionId,
    pub actor_id: ActorId,
    pub authorization_id: AuthorizationId,
    pub source_watermark: WatermarkId,
    pub effect_type: EffectType,
    pub target: EffectTarget,
    pub observed_at: Timestamp,
    pub evidence_root: EvidenceRoot,
    pub provenance_root: ProvenanceRoot,
    pub reversibility: Reversibility,
    pub containment_status: ContainmentStatus,
}

The system can therefore distinguish:

ACTION

from:

EFFECT

This distinction is foundational.


---

III. ⚖️ ACTION ≠ EFFECT

An action is:

> what the agent did.



An effect is:

> what changed because the action occurred.



Therefore:

ACTION A
    ↓
EFFECT E

is not necessarily:

A = E

One action may produce:

E1
E2
E3

and one effect may have multiple causal contributors.

PALACO must preserve that distinction.


---

IV. 🧬 EFFECT PROVENANCE

Every material effect must answer:

WHO?
WHAT?
WHEN?
UNDER WHICH AUTHORITY?
UNDER WHICH DUTY?
UNDER WHICH RULESET?
FROM WHICH WATERMARK?
TO WHICH TARGET?
WITH WHICH EVIDENCE?

Canonical chain:

CONSTITUTION
 ↓
RULESET
 ↓
AUTHORITY
 ↓
DUTY
 ↓
COMMAND
 ↓
ACTION
 ↓
EFFECT
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
PROVENANCE
 ↓
WATERMARK


---

V. 🚨 EFFECT AFTER REVOCATION

Suppose:

W10
 ↓
AUTHORIZED ACTION
 ↓
EFFECT E10
 ↓
W11
 ↓
AUTHORITY REVOKED

The revocation does not retroactively invalidate the fact that:

E10 occurred.

Instead PALACO records:

E10
STATUS = OCCURRED
AUTHORIZATION_AT_EFFECT = VALID
CURRENT_AUTHORIZATION = REVOKED

This distinction prevents historical corruption.


---

VI. 🔐 EFFECT VALIDITY VS EFFECT CONSEQUENCE

Two questions must be separated:

Question A

> Was the action constitutionally valid when the effect occurred?



Question B

> What should happen to the effect now?



These are different adjudications.

Possible:

ACTION_VALID_AT_T₀
+
EFFECT_IRREVERSIBLE

The system may therefore conclude:

HISTORICALLY_VALID
CURRENTLY_UNDESIRED

That is not a contradiction.


---

VII. 🌳 REVERSIBILITY CLASSIFICATION

pub enum Reversibility {
    Reversible,
    Compensatable,
    Containable,
    PartiallyReversible,
    Irreversible,
    Unknown,
}

Critical rule:

Unknown ≠ Reversible

The system must never assume that an effect can be undone.


---

VIII. 🛑 EFFECT CONTAINMENT

When an effect cannot safely be reversed immediately:

EFFECT DETECTED
      ↓
CONTAINMENT
      ↓
ISOLATION
      ↓
STATE PRESERVATION
      ↓
ASSESSMENT

Containment may include:

stop propagation
quarantine dependent state
freeze further mutation
isolate affected resource
prevent cascading actions
preserve evidence

The precise mechanism is domain-specific.

The constitutional requirement is not.

UNCONTROLLED PROPAGATION MUST NOT BE ALLOWED WHEN CONTAINMENT IS REQUIRED.


---

IX. 🔥 CASCADING EFFECTS

A particularly dangerous case:

ACTION A
 ↓
EFFECT E1
 ↓
AGENT B
 ↓
ACTION B
 ↓
EFFECT E2
 ↓
AGENT C
 ↓
ACTION C
 ↓
EFFECT E3

When A is revoked, PALACO must not assume:

E1 → E2 → E3

are automatically invalid.

Instead it constructs a causal graph:

A
│
└── E1
     │
     └── B
          │
          └── E2
               │
               └── C
                    │
                    └── E3

Then determines the constitutional status of each node.


---

X. 🧠 BRAINPOWER EFFECT GRAPH

BRAINPOWER may calculate:

causal dependencies
downstream effects
affected actors
affected resources
containment candidates
recovery candidates

But:

> BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT rewrite causal history merely because a later outcome appears preferable.



It can propose:

POSSIBLE_RECOVERY_PATH

not declare:

RECOVERY_PROVEN


---

XI. 🦆 FOOL EFFECT CHALLENGE

FOOL gains:

EFFECT_CHALLENGE

Possible challenges:

UNATTRIBUTED_EFFECT
MISSING_EFFECT
FALSE_REVERSIBILITY
HIDDEN_CASCADE
BROKEN_PROVENANCE
UNPROVEN_RECOVERY
UNCONTAINED_PROPAGATION
INCORRECT_CAUSAL_LINK
POST_REVOCATION_EFFECT

FOOL therefore protects against a particularly dangerous failure:

> pretending that consequences disappeared merely because authorization disappeared.




---

XII. 🔬 TRIAS EFFECT VERIFICATION

TRIAS verifies:

Action identity
Authorization state
Duty state
Effect identity
Effect timing
Effect target
Causal relationship
Evidence
Provenance
Reversibility classification
Containment result
Recovery result
Watermark continuity

TRIAS does not decide whether the outcome is morally desirable.

It determines whether the claim about what happened and what followed is provable.


---

XIII. ⚓ QUAY

The Quay now becomes the historical memory not only of actions, but consequences:

ACTION
 ↓
EFFECT
 ↓
CONTAINMENT
 ↓
RECOVERY
 ↓
RECONCILIATION

Nothing is silently removed.

A failed recovery remains a historical event.

An unsuccessful rollback remains evidence.

An irreversible consequence remains visible.


---

XIV. 💧 WATERMARKED EFFECTS

Every material effect transition receives temporal anchoring:

W20
 ↓
ACTION
 ↓
EFFECT
 ↓
W21

If containment occurs:

W21
 ↓
CONTAINMENT
 ↓
W22

If compensation occurs:

W22
 ↓
COMPENSATION
 ↓
W23

Thus:

THE EFFECT HISTORY BECOMES PART OF CONSTITUTIONAL MEMORY.


---

XV. 🔄 ROLLBACK

Rollback is only one possible recovery mechanism.

EFFECT
 ↓
ROLLBACK
 ↓
RESTORED STATE

But PALACO must prove that restoration actually occurred.

Therefore:

Claim:
"Rollback succeeded."

requires:

BEFORE_STATE
+
ROLLBACK_EVENT
+
AFTER_STATE
+
STATE_COMPARISON
+
EVIDENCE

A rollback command alone is not proof of rollback success.


---

XVI. 🩹 COMPENSATING RECOVERY

Sometimes exact rollback is impossible.

Then:

EFFECT
 ↓
IRREVERSIBLE
 ↓
COMPENSATION

Compensation does not rewrite history.

It creates a new constitutional event.

Example:

E1 = irreversible loss
 ↓
C1 = compensating action

The record remains:

E1 OCCURRED
C1 FOLLOWED

not:

E1 NEVER OCCURRED


---

XVII. 💀 IRREVERSIBLE EFFECT

When an effect cannot be undone:

pub enum RecoveryResult {
    RolledBack,
    Compensated,
    Contained,
    PartiallyRecovered,
    Irrecoverable,
    RecoveryFailed,
    RecoveryNotRequired,
}

Irrecoverable is not a system failure by itself.

It is a truthful constitutional state.

The failure would be claiming:

RECOVERED

when recovery cannot be proven.


---

XVIII. 🚫 NO FICTIONAL ROLLBACK

Forbidden:

EFFECT
 ↓
RECOVERY ATTEMPT
 ↓
"ROLLBACK SUCCESS"

without evidence.

Canonical principle:

A RECOVERY CLAIM REQUIRES RECOVERY PROOF.


---

XIX. 🧭 EFFECT RECONCILIATION

After an interruption:

ACTION
 ↓
EFFECT
 ↓
REVOCATION

PALACO enters:

EFFECT_RECONCILIATION

Possible result:

VALID_AND_PRESERVED
VALID_AND_COMPENSATED
CONTAINED
PARTIALLY_RECOVERED
INVALID_AND_REVERSED
INVALID_AND_IRREVERSIBLE
UNRESOLVED


---

XX. ⚖️ VALID ACTION, INVALID CURRENT STATE

An especially important case:

ACTION VALID

but:

CURRENT STATE = NO LONGER DESIRED

The system must not confuse:

constitutional validity

with:

present policy preference

A historically valid effect can later require remediation without being reclassified as historically fabricated.


---

XXI. 🌐 FEDERATED EFFECTS

An effect may cross Citadel boundaries:

CITADEL A
   ↓
EFFECT
   ↓
CITADEL B

Each domain maintains its own provenance.

The federated record becomes:

A-W10
   ↓
DIPLOMATIC / FEDERATED EVENT
   ↓
B-W22
   ↓
F-W3

The federation creates a reconciliation anchor.

It does not erase either source history.


---

XXII. 🏛️ LA PAZ

Suppose:

LPZ-W40
 ↓
AUTHORIZED ACTION
 ↓
EXTERNAL EFFECT
 ↓
PLANETARY REVOCATION

La Paz must preserve:

LPZ-W40

and the external effect.

It cannot simply rewrite:

LPZ-W40

because the planetary layer later disagreed.

Instead:

LPZ-W40
 ↓
EFFECT
 ↓
DIPLOMATIC EVENT
 ↓
LPZ-W41

The histories remain distinct but interoperable.


---

XXIII. 🔱 EFFECT AUTHORITY

A subtle but important principle:

The authority to perform an action does not automatically imply authority to remediate every consequence.

Therefore:

ACTION_AUTHORITY
≠
RECOVERY_AUTHORITY

Recovery may require:

new authorization
new duty
new jurisdiction
new evidence

This prevents an agent from acquiring unlimited post-action power simply because it caused the original effect.


---

XXIV. ⏳ RECOVERY DEADLINES

Some effects require time-bounded remediation.

EFFECT
 ↓
RECOVERY_WINDOW
 ↓
EXPIRY

After expiry:

RECOVERY = LATE

The system must record that fact.

It must not pretend the recovery occurred within the original window.


---

XXV. 🔬 DETERMINISTIC EFFECT REPLAY

R6.57 extends the Proof Machine:

Replay(
    Constitution,
    Rulesets,
    Authorities,
    Duties,
    Commands,
    Actions,
    Effects,
    Revocations,
    RecoveryEvents
)
→ HistoricalOutcome

The verifier must reproduce:

ACTION
+
EFFECT
+
AUTHORITY STATUS
+
CONTAINMENT
+
RECOVERY

If not:

EFFECT_REPLAY_DIVERGENCE


---

XXVI. 🚨 FIRST EFFECT DIVERGENCE

Suppose:

W30 ✓
W31 ✓
W32 ✓
EFFECT E7 ✕

The Proof Machine reports:

FIRST_EFFECT_DIVERGENCE = E7

This is materially more useful than:

REPLAY FAILED

because it identifies the first disputed consequence.


---

XXVII. 🧬 EFFECT LINEAGE

R6.20's lineage concept now extends naturally:

LINEAGE
 ↓
WATERMARK
 ↓
ACTION
 ↓
EFFECT
 ↓
RECOVERY
 ↓
NEW STATE

An evolved system must inherit not merely:

WHAT THE OLD SYSTEM WAS

but:

WHAT EFFECTS THE OLD SYSTEM CREATED

This will become crucial for R6.58+.


---

XXVIII. 🛡️ EFFECT CONTAINMENT GATE

Before an action is allowed to produce high-impact external effects:

Authority        PASS
Duty             PASS
Live validity    PASS
Effect model     PASS
Reversibility    PASS
Containment      PASS
Evidence         PASS
Provenance       PASS
Watermark        PASS

Otherwise:

BLOCK

For certain actions, the system must additionally prove:

recovery capability

before execution.


---

XXIX. 🌱 PRE-COMMIT EFFECT DECLARATION

Where feasible, the actor should declare expected effects before execution:

pub struct ExpectedEffect {
    pub effect_type: EffectType,
    pub target: EffectTarget,
    pub expected_scope: EffectScope,
    pub reversibility: Reversibility,
}

After execution:

EXPECTED EFFECT
        ↓
ACTUAL EFFECT
        ↓
COMPARE

Unexpected material effects produce:

UNDECLARED_EFFECT

and trigger investigation.


---

XXX. 🚨 UNDECLARED EFFECT

An action may be authorized while producing an effect outside its declared scope.

Example:

AUTHORIZED:
modify X

Actual:

X modified
Y modified
Z triggered

Then:

Y
Z

require separate attribution and constitutional evaluation.

Authorization for X does not automatically authorize Y and Z.


---

XXXI. 🔥 THE EFFECT BOUNDARY

R6.57 establishes:

AUTHORIZATION MUST BOUND NOT ONLY ACTION, BUT EXPECTED CONSEQUENCE.

Therefore:

AUTHORITY
 ↓
DUTY
 ↓
ACTION SCOPE
 ↓
EFFECT SCOPE

A system cannot evade constitutional boundaries by treating consequences as someone else's problem.


---

XXXII. 🔱 R6.57 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.57-I01
Every material constitutional action SHALL have attributable effects where effects occur.

R6.57-I02
Action SHALL remain distinguishable from effect.

R6.57-I03
Every material effect SHALL be attributable to a causal action or explicitly classified as unproven.

R6.57-I04
Every material effect SHALL be evidence-bound.

R6.57-I05
Every material effect SHALL be provenance-bound.

R6.57-I06
Every material effect SHALL be temporally anchored.

R6.57-I07
Effect reversibility SHALL NOT be assumed.

R6.57-I08
Unknown reversibility SHALL NOT be treated as reversibility.

R6.57-I09
Revocation SHALL NOT erase effects that already occurred.

R6.57-I10
Historical validity SHALL remain distinguishable from present desirability.

R6.57-I11
Material effects SHALL support containment where constitutionally required.

R6.57-I12
Containment SHALL itself be auditable.

R6.57-I13
Rollback SHALL require proof of restored state.

R6.57-I14
Compensation SHALL be recorded as a new constitutional event.

R6.57-I15
Compensation SHALL NOT rewrite historical effects.

R6.57-I16
Irreversible effects SHALL be explicitly represented.

R6.57-I17
Irrecoverable effects SHALL remain historically preserved.

R6.57-I18
Recovery claims SHALL require recovery evidence.

R6.57-I19
An action authority SHALL NOT automatically confer recovery authority.

R6.57-I20
Unexpected material effects SHALL be separately evaluated.

R6.57-I21
Undeclared effects SHALL NOT inherit authorization automatically.

R6.57-I22
Cascading effects SHALL preserve causal relationships.

R6.57-I23
Federated effects SHALL preserve source-domain provenance.

R6.57-I24
Federated reconciliation SHALL NOT erase source histories.

R6.57-I25
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge effect attribution and recovery claims.

R6.57-I26
BRAINPOWER SHALL identify possible causal chains without fabricating causality.

R6.57-I27
TRIAS SHALL independently verify material effect claims.

R6.57-I28
Material effects SHALL be recorded through the Quay.

R6.57-I29
Material effect transitions SHALL be watermarked.

R6.57-I30
Effect histories SHALL be independently replayable.

R6.57-I31
The first effect divergence SHALL be independently identifiable.

R6.57-I32
A constitutional interruption SHALL NOT terminate the obligation to account for effects already produced.

R6.57-I33
No recovery process SHALL silently destroy the evidence of the original effect.

R6.57-I34
Containment SHALL prevent unauthorized propagation where technically and constitutionally required.

R6.57-I35
The system SHALL distinguish reversal, compensation, containment, and irrecoverability.

R6.57-I36
No actor SHALL claim that an effect did not occur merely because its originating authorization was later revoked.

R6.57-I37
Effect consequences SHALL remain attributable across lineage transitions.

R6.57-I38
A successor system SHALL NOT inherit unresolved effects without explicit provenance.

R6.57-I39
External effects SHALL remain constitutionally accountable after execution terminates.

R6.57-I40
No irreversible effect SHALL become an invisible historical state.


---

XXXIII. ☄️ THE R6 CONTINUITY MACHINE

We now have:

GENESIS
   ↓
WATERMARK
   ↓
LINEAGE
   ↓
EVOLUTION
   ↓
JURISDICTION
   ↓
