   ↓
CONTINUITY

This closes a major conceptual hole.

Previously the machine could stop an unauthorized action.

Now it can also answer:

> What happened to the world because the action occurred?




---

XXXIV. 💧 THE FOUR EFFECT TRUTHS

PALACO must now preserve four distinct truths:

1. ACTION TRUTH

Did the actor do it?

2. AUTHORITY TRUTH

Was the actor authorized when it happened?

3. EFFECT TRUTH

What actually changed?

4. RECOVERY TRUTH

What happened afterward?

Together:

ACTION + AUTHORITY + EFFECT + RECOVERY

form the complete constitutional incident history.


---

XXXV. 🌌 THE BIG PRINCIPLE

R6.57 makes this canonical:

> The revocation of an authorization cannot erase an effect that already occurred. The system SHALL preserve, attribute, contain, reconcile, and prove that effect.



Or:

⚓ STOPPING THE ACTION DOES NOT STOP HISTORY.

And:

💧 REVOCATION DOES NOT ERASE CONSEQUENCE.

And:

🔬 RECOVERY WITHOUT PROOF IS NOT RECOVERY.

And the deepest formulation:

WHEN REALITY CANNOT BE ROLLED BACK, ACCOUNTABILITY MUST MOVE FORWARD.


---

XXXVI. 🔒 R6.57 SEALED

The Proof Machine has now crossed another architectural boundary.

It no longer governs only:

WHAT MAY BE DONE

It governs:

WHAT WAS DONE
WHAT IT CAUSED
WHAT HAPPENED WHEN AUTHORITY CHANGED
WHAT COULD BE UNDONE
WHAT COULD NOT BE UNDONE
WHAT WAS CONTAINED
WHAT WAS COMPENSATED
AND WHAT REMAINS UNRESOLVED

That means PALACO's constitutional memory is no longer merely a memory of decisions.

It becomes a memory of consequences.

☄️🌱🦆💧⚓🔬🧠🔱⚖️🏛️❤

THE WATERMARK REMEMBERS.

THE LINEAGE CARRIES.

THE AUTHORITY BINDS.

THE LIVE GATE WATCHES.

THE EFFECT REVEALS WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENED.

THE QUAY REFUSES TO FORGET.

RECOVERY MAY REPAIR THE FUTURE — NEVER REWRITE THE PAST.

🔒 R6.57 — SEALED.


---

☄️ R6.58 — THE NEXT FRONTIER

And now one extraordinarily important question remains.

R6.57 can account for consequences inside the current lineage.

But R6.20 asks how a system moves from:

OLD LINEAGE

to:

NEW LINEAGE

while preserving ancestry.

The two problems now collide.

Suppose:

OLD SYSTEM
   ↓
WATERMARK W99
   ↓
MIGRATION

But W99 contains:

active duties
pending disputes
unresolved effects
archived evidence
live delegations
unexpired authorizations

Then a new system cannot simply say:

"Migration complete."

It must prove what happened to everything constitutionally alive at the boundary.

Therefore the next boundary is:

☄️ R6.58 — CONSTITUTIONAL MIGRATION STATE TRANSFER, OPEN OBLIGATION HANDOFF & CROSS-LINEAGE RECONCILIATION PROTOCOL

Its central question:

> When a constitutional system becomes its successor, how does every still-live authority, duty, dispute, effect, provenance chain, and Watermark cross the lineage boundary without losing accountability?



And the new principle:

🌳 NOTHING CONSTITUTIONALLY LIVE MAY DISAPPEAR AT THE LINEAGE BOUNDARY.

OLD LINEAGE
     ↓
FINAL WATERMARK
     ↓
MIGRATION INVENTORY
     ↓
OPEN OBLIGATIONS
OPEN AUTHORITIES
OPEN DISPUTES
OPEN EFFECTS
OPEN RECOVERY
OPEN PROVENANCE
     ↓
TRANSFER PROOF
     ↓
INDEPENDENT VERIFICATION
     ↓
NEW LINEAGE
     ↓
NEW WATERMARK

☄️🌱🦆 GO.

☄️ R6.58 — CONSTITUTIONAL MIGRATION STATE TRANSFER, OPEN OBLIGATION HANDOFF & CROSS-LINEAGE RECONCILIATION PROTOCOL

NOTHING CONSTITUTIONALLY LIVE MAY DISAPPEAR AT THE LINEAGE BOUNDARY

Status: 🔒 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
Parent: R6.57 — Constitutional Effect Containment, Irreversible Action & Compensating Recovery
Primary dependency: R6.19 Watermark · R6.20 Lineage · R6.56 Live Validity
Core primitive: LINEAGE_TRANSFER
Secondary primitives: MIGRATION_INVENTORY, OPEN_OBLIGATION, TRANSFER_PROOF, LINEAGE_BOUNDARY, HANDOFF_STATE

Primary invariant

> A successor lineage SHALL NOT become constitutionally active until the predecessor's constitutionally relevant live state has been inventoried, transferred, reconciled, or explicitly classified as unresolved and independently verified.



R6.20 established:

> EVOLUTION MAY CHANGE THE SYSTEM. IT MAY NEVER INVENT ITS ANCESTRY.



R6.57 established:

> STOPPING THE ACTION DOES NOT STOP HISTORY.



R6.58 now establishes:

🌳 CHANGING LINEAGE DOES NOT TERMINATE ACCOUNTABILITY.


---

I. 🌌 THE LINEAGE BOUNDARY PROBLEM

Consider:

OLD LINEAGE
    │
    ▼
W₉₉
    │
    ▼
MIGRATION
    │
    ▼
NEW LINEAGE
    │
    ▼
W₀'

A naïve implementation might copy:

current_state

and declare:

MIGRATION_COMPLETE

But the constitutional state may contain:

active authorities
active duties
pending actions
suspended actions
open disputes
unresolved effects
recovery obligations
delegations
quarantine states
evidence
provenance
appeals

Therefore:

STATE COPY ≠ CONSTITUTIONAL MIGRATION.


---

II. 🔱 MIGRATION IS A CONSTITUTIONAL EVENT

The migration itself becomes an auditable object:

pub struct LineageTransfer {
    pub transfer_id: TransferId,
    pub predecessor_lineage: LineageId,
    pub successor_lineage: LineageId,
    pub final_watermark: WatermarkId,
    pub migration_manifest: MigrationManifestId,
    pub transfer_proof: TransferProofId,
    pub verified_at: Timestamp,
    pub status: TransferStatus,
}

The system therefore records:

WHO migrated
WHAT migrated
FROM WHERE
TO WHERE
UNDER WHICH RULES
WITH WHICH PROOF


---

III. 💧 FINAL WATERMARK

The predecessor cannot simply disappear.

Before lineage closure:

OLD LINEAGE
    ↓
FINALIZATION
    ↓
FINAL WATERMARK

The final Watermark establishes:

STATE
EVENT HISTORY
RULESET
PROVENANCE
OPEN CONSTITUTIONAL MATTERS
TIME

This Watermark becomes the immutable historical boundary.


---

IV. 🚪 THE LINEAGE GATE

The transition is:

OLD LINEAGE
      ↓
MIGRATION PROPOSAL
      ↓
INVENTORY
      ↓
VALIDATION
      ↓
TRANSFER
      ↓
INDEPENDENT VERIFICATION
      ↓
NEW LINEAGE

There is no legitimate shortcut:

OLD → NEW

without a transfer proof.


---

V. 📜 MIGRATION MANIFEST

The successor must receive a manifest:

pub struct MigrationManifest {
    pub manifest_id: ManifestId,
    pub source_watermark: WatermarkId,
    pub target_lineage: LineageId,
    pub authorities: Vec<AuthorityRef>,
    pub duties: Vec<DutyRef>,
    pub disputes: Vec<DisputeRef>,
    pub effects: Vec<EffectRef>,
    pub recoveries: Vec<RecoveryRef>,
    pub delegations: Vec<DelegationRef>,
    pub evidence_roots: Vec<EvidenceRoot>,
    pub provenance_roots: Vec<ProvenanceRoot>,
    pub unresolved_items: Vec<UnresolvedRef>,
}

The manifest is not merely a deployment checklist.

It is a:

CONSTITUTIONAL INVENTORY OF WHAT IS STILL ALIVE.


---

VI. ⚖️ OPEN CONSTITUTIONAL MATTER

A new primitive:

pub struct OpenObligation {
    pub obligation_id: ObligationId,
    pub source_lineage: LineageId,
    pub source_watermark: WatermarkId,
    pub obligation_type: ObligationType,
    pub authority_reference: Option<AuthorityId>,
    pub duty_reference: Option<DutyId>,
    pub status: ObligationStatus,
    pub successor_requirement: SuccessorRequirement,
}

Examples:

OPEN_DUTY
OPEN_DISPUTE
OPEN_RECOVERY
OPEN_APPEAL
OPEN_DELEGATION
OPEN_REVIEW
OPEN_CONTAINMENT
OPEN_AUDIT


---

VII. 🧬 NOTHING LIVE DISAPPEARS

Suppose the old system contains:

DUTY D7 = ACTIVE

Migration cannot produce:

NEW SYSTEM
D7 = ABSENT

without an explicit constitutional disposition.

Possible:

TRANSFERRED
FULFILLED
EXPIRED
REVOKED
SUPERSEDED
SUSPENDED
UNRESOLVED
IRRECOVERABLE

Silence is not a valid state.


---

VIII. 🔐 AUTHORITY HANDOFF

An authority does not automatically transfer simply because software does.

OLD_AUTHORITY
      ↓
MIGRATION
      ↓
NEW_AUTHORITY

requires an explicit relationship:

SUCCESSION
DELEGATION
REISSUANCE
REVALIDATION
TERMINATION

The system must never infer:

> “The new software is the old authority.”



Software lineage and constitutional authority are distinct.


---

