---

I. 🌌 THE FORK PROBLEM

A constitutional system may legitimately diverge.

For example:

L₀
                    │
                   W₀
                    │
             ┌──────┴──────┐
             ▼             ▼
           L₁-A           L₁-B
             │             │
            W-A           W-B

This can occur because of:

different jurisdictions;

independent Citadels;

competing constitutional proposals;

temporary federation splits;

disaster recovery;

incompatible evolution paths;

deliberate constitutional experimentation.


The problem is not branching.

The problem is historical ambiguity.

PALACO must never allow:

L₁-A

to claim:

"I alone am the original continuation"

unless that claim is provable.


---

II. 🔱 FORK ≠ COPY

A fork is not:

COPY DATABASE

It is:

