XVIII. ⚖️ DELEGATED AUTHORITY

Authority can legitimately cross domains when explicitly established:

A
 │
 └── DELEGATES SCOPE X → B

The delegation requires:

scope
duration
conditions
evidence
authority proof
revocation rules

Therefore:

AUTHORITY CAN CROSS A BORDER ONLY THROUGH PROVEN CONSTITUTIONAL MECHANISM.


