Delegated authority SHALL be revocable where constitutionally permitted.

R6.61-I22
Federation SHALL preserve source lineages.

R6.61-I23
Federated relationships SHALL be independently recorded.

R6.61-I24
Federated Watermarks SHALL NOT replace source Watermarks.

R6.61-I25
Cross-domain cooperation SHALL NOT imply constitutional merger.

R6.61-I26
Cross-domain disagreement SHALL NOT imply invalidity.

R6.61-I27
Recognition MAY coexist with contest.

R6.61-I28
Multiple sovereign domains MAY possess simultaneous canonical presents.

R6.61-I29
BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT infer sovereignty from technical control.

R6.61-I30
BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT infer trust from statistical similarity alone.

R6.61-I31
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge recognition.

R6.61-I32
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge cross-domain authority.

R6.61-I33
TRIAS SHALL verify sovereignty boundaries.

R6.61-I34
TRIAS SHALL verify recognition claims.

R6.61-I35
TRIAS SHALL verify trust assertions.

R6.61-I36
The Quay SHALL preserve diplomatic history.

R6.61-I37
The Quay SHALL preserve cross-domain provenance.

R6.61-I38
Termination SHALL NOT erase relationship history.

R6.61-I39
Historical recognition SHALL remain distinguishable from current recognition.

R6.61-I40
No domain SHALL declare jurisdiction over another domain solely by recognition.


---

XLII. 🌐 THE SOVEREIGNTY EQUATION

Conceptually:

SOVEREIGNTY =
IDENTITY
+
LINEAGE
+
CANONICAL WATERMARK
+
AUTHORITY SCOPE
+
CONSTITUTIONAL PROOF

Recognition becomes:

RECOGNITION =
IDENTITY PROOF
+
LINEAGE PROOF
+
WATERMARK PROOF
+
RELATIONSHIP DECISION

Trust becomes:

TRUST =
SUBJECT
+
SCOPE
+
EVIDENCE
+
CONDITIONS
+
TIME

Federation becomes:

FEDERATION =
SOVEREIGN A
+
SOVEREIGN B
+
AGREEMENT
+
SCOPE
+
EVIDENCE
+
RELATIONSHIP WATERMARK


---

XLIII. 🔱 THE BIG PRINCIPLE

R6.61 makes canonical:

> Constitutional domains MAY recognize, trust, cooperate, delegate authority to, or federate with one another without surrendering their independent lineage or sovereignty. Every cross-domain authority relationship SHALL be explicit, scoped, temporally valid where applicable, evidence-bound, and independently verifiable.



Or, even shorter:

🌐 RECOGNITION WITHOUT SUBORDINATION.

⚓ COOPERATION WITHOUT MERGER.

🔐 TRUST WITHOUT BLINDNESS.

🔱 AUTHORITY WITHOUT SCOPE ESCALATION.

🌳 PLURALITY WITHOUT HISTORICAL AMNESIA.


---

XLIV. 🔒 R6.61 SEALED

The architecture now has a remarkably complete constitutional topology:

CONSTITUTION
                              │
                           RULESET
                              │
                           MANDATE
                              │
                            ACTION
                              │
                           EVIDENCE
                              │
                         PROVENANCE
                              │
                            EVENT
                              │
                            QUAY
                              │
                         WATERMARK
                              │
                           REPLAY
                              │
                       SECOND WITNESS
                              │
                          CHALLENGE
                              │
                        ADJUDICATION
                              │
                          CORRECTION
                              │
                        NEW WATERMARK
                              │
                          CONTINUITY
                              │
                           LINEAGE
                              │
                           BRANCH
                         ╱       ╲
                    SUCCESSION   FORK
                         ╲       ╱
                           MERGE
                              │
                     CANONICAL PRESENT
                              │
                         SOVEREIGNTY
                              │
                       RECOGNITION
                              │
                            TRUST
                              │
                         DIPLOMACY
                              │
                         FEDERATION

And one sentence captures the new layer:

A CONSTITUTIONAL BORDER IS NOT A WALL OF IGNORANCE; IT IS A PROVABLE BOUNDARY OF AUTHORITY.

☄️🌱🦆💧⚓🔬🧠🔱🏛️❤

THE WATERMARK REMEMBERS.

THE LINEAGE CONNECTS.

THE BRANCH DECLARES DIVERGENCE.

THE CANONICAL PRESENT DECLARES CURRENT AUTHORITY.

SOVEREIGNTY DECLARES THE BOUNDARY.

RECOGNITION CROSSES THE BOUNDARY WITHOUT ERASING IT.

🔒 R6.61 — SEALED.


---

☄️ R6.62 — THE NEXT FRONTIER

Now a subtle but decisive problem emerges.

If multiple sovereign domains can:

recognize
trust
cooperate
delegate
federate

then eventually they will encounter evidence that crosses constitutional borders.

For example:

A-W100
   │
   └── Evidence E-A
             │
             ▼
         B-W200
             │
             └── Evidence E-B

What happens when:

A claims one fact;

B claims another;

both have valid Watermarks;

both have valid evidence;

both have legitimate authority within their own domains;

and the two claims interact?


The answer cannot simply be:

A wins

or:

B wins

or:

majority wins

Because PALACO's foundational principle remains:

> The objective is not to manufacture agreement. The objective is to establish what can actually be proven.



That points directly toward:

☄️ R6.62 — CROSS-LINEAGE EVIDENCE RECOGNITION, EVIDENTIARY INTEROPERABILITY & CONSTITUTIONAL FACT RECONCILIATION PROTOCOL

Emerging principle:

🔬 DOMAINS MAY DISAGREE ON CONSTITUTIONAL MEANING WHILE STILL AGREEING ON PROVABLE FACTS.

And perhaps the most important distinction yet:

FACT
≠
INTERPRETATION
≠
AUTHORITY
≠
CONSENT

☄️🌱🦆 GO

☄️ R6.62 — CROSS-LINEAGE EVIDENCE RECOGNITION, EVIDENTIARY INTEROPERABILITY & CONSTITUTIONAL FACT RECONCILIATION PROTOCOL

FACT CAN CROSS A BORDER WITHOUT AUTHORITY CROSSING WITH IT

Status: 🔒 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
Parent: R6.61 — Constitutional Sovereignty, Cross-Lineage Recognition & Diplomatic Trust Protocol
Core primitive: EVIDENCE_CLAIM
Supporting primitives: FACT_CLAIM, INTERPRETATION_CLAIM, RECOGNITION_SCOPE, RECONCILIATION_RESULT, EVIDENCE_BRIDGE

Primary invariant

> A constitutional domain SHALL be able to recognize externally produced evidence without thereby recognizing the external authority, interpretation, or constitutional jurisdiction that produced it.



This is the next major distinction.

R6.61 established:

🌐 RECOGNITION WITHOUT SUBORDINATION.

R6.62 now establishes:

🔬 EVIDENCE WITHOUT AUTHORITY TRANSFER.


---

I. 🌌 THE PROBLEM OF CROSS-LINEAGE TRUTH

Consider:

CITADEL A                         CITADEL B

A-W100                            B-W200
   │                                 │
   ▼                                 ▼
Evidence EA                     Evidence EB
   │                                 │
   └──────────────┬──────────────────┘
                  ▼
             RECONCILIATION

Both domains may possess:

valid lineage
valid Watermark
valid evidence
valid authority

Yet they may disagree about what those facts mean.

Therefore PALACO must distinguish:

WHAT HAPPENED?

from:

WHAT DOES IT MEAN?

and from:

WHO HAS AUTHORITY TO DECIDE?

These are three different constitutional questions.


---

II. 🔱 FOUR LAYERS OF CLAIM

R6.62 introduces:

FACT
  ↓
EVIDENCE
  ↓
INTERPRETATION
  ↓
AUTHORITY

More precisely:

1. FACT_CLAIM

> Something happened.



2. EVIDENCE_CLAIM

> Here is the evidence supporting that claim.



3. INTERPRETATION_CLAIM

> Under this constitutional framework, that fact means X.



4. AUTHORITY_CLAIM

> This actor/domain is entitled to act upon that interpretation.



These SHALL NOT be conflated.


---

III. 🧬 FACT CLAIM

Conceptually:

pub struct FactClaim {
    pub claim_id: ClaimId,
    pub subject: SubjectRef,
    pub proposition: Proposition,
    pub evidence_root: EvidenceRoot,
    pub source_domain: DomainId,
    pub source_watermark: WatermarkId,
    pub temporal_scope: TemporalScope,
}

A fact claim must identify:

who asserts it
what is asserted
when it applies
which evidence supports it
under which Watermark it was recorded


---

IV. 🔬 EVIDENCE CLAIM

Evidence is not identical to the proposition it supports.

Therefore:

pub struct EvidenceClaim {
    pub evidence_id: EvidenceId,
    pub claim_id: ClaimId,
    pub evidence_type: EvidenceType,
    pub provenance_root: ProvenanceRoot,
    pub integrity_proof: IntegrityProof,
    pub source_watermark: WatermarkId,
}

This gives PALACO:

CLAIM
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
PROVENANCE
 ↓
WATERMARK


---

V. 🚫 EVIDENCE ≠ TRUTH

A domain may possess valid evidence for a claim without that evidence proving the claim absolutely.

Therefore:

VALID EVIDENCE

means:

> the evidence itself is authentic, intact, attributable, and admissible within the applicable framework.



It does not automatically mean:

CLAIM = UNIVERSALLY TRUE

This distinction is essential.


---

VI. 🌐 EXTERNAL EVIDENCE

Suppose:

A → EA

and B receives EA.

B may verify:

signature
hash
provenance
Watermark
source lineage
temporal validity

B may then conclude:

EA = AUTHENTIC

without concluding:

A = CONSTITUTIONAL AUTHORITY OVER B

Thus:

AUTHENTICITY MAY CROSS THE BORDER WITHOUT AUTHORITY CROSSING THE BORDER.


---

VII. ⚓ EVIDENCE BRIDGE

Introduce:

pub struct EvidenceBridge {
    pub bridge_id: EvidenceBridgeId,
    pub source_domain: DomainId,
    pub source_watermark: WatermarkId,
    pub receiving_domain: DomainId,
    pub evidence_root: EvidenceRoot,
    pub verification_result: VerificationResult,
    pub recognition_scope: RecognitionScope,
}

The bridge records:

A's evidence

as received by:

B

without making B's history a continuation of A's history.


---

VIII. 💧 WATERMARK-PRESERVING TRANSFER

When:

A-W100

sends evidence to:

B-W200

B records:

A-W100 → EvidenceBridge → B-W200

not:

A-W100 → B-W200

as a lineage transition.

This preserves:

SOURCE HISTORY + RECEIVING HISTORY.


---

IX. 🧠 CROSS-LINEAGE RECONCILIATION

Now consider:

A claims:
EVENT X occurred at T1.

B claims:
EVENT X occurred at T2.

Both claims may have evidence.

PALACO does not immediately select one.

Instead:

CLAIM A
   ↓
EVIDENCE A
   ↓
CLAIM B
   ↓
EVIDENCE B
   ↓
TEMPORAL ANALYSIS
   ↓
PROVENANCE ANALYSIS
   ↓
DEPENDENCY ANALYSIS
   ↓
RECONCILIATION


---

X. 🔬 RECONCILIATION OUTCOMES

The result may be:

AGREED
PARTIALLY_AGREED
COMPATIBLE
INCOMPATIBLE
UNRESOLVED
CONTRADICTORY
INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE
OUT_OF_SCOPE

Crucially:

UNRESOLVED IS A VALID RESULT.


---

XI. 🚫 NO FORCED CONSENSUS

Forbidden:

A says X
B says Y
     ↓
SYSTEM
     ↓
X AND Y COMPROMISE

A constitutional proof system does not manufacture an intermediate truth.

Instead:

A = supported
B = supported
relationship = unresolved

may be the correct result.


---

XII. 🌳 FACT RECONCILIATION

Suppose:

A:
"Event E occurred."

B:
"Event E occurred."

Both agree on the fact.

But:

A:
"E was authorized."

B:
"E was unauthorized."

Then:

FACT = AGREED
INTERPRETATION = DISPUTED
AUTHORITY = DISPUTED

This is much more precise than saying:

"the domains disagree."


---

XIII. 🔱 THE FOUR-STATE DISTINCTION

PALACO can therefore represent:

FACT_STATUS
INTERPRETATION_STATUS
AUTHORITY_STATUS
CONSENT_STATUS

Example:

FACT            = PROVEN
INTERPRETATION  = CONTESTED
AUTHORITY       = UNPROVEN
CONSENT         = ABSENT

That is a legitimate constitutional state.


---

XIV. ⚖️ FACT DOES NOT CREATE CONSENT

If:

A proves:
"B received message X."

this does not establish:

B consented to X.

Likewise:

A proves:
"B performed action Y."

does not establish:

B authorized Y.

Therefore:

OBSERVATION ≠ CONSENT.


---

XV. 🛡️ AUTHORITY CLAIM

An authority claim must reference:

constitution
mandate
scope
lineage
Watermark
evidence

Conceptually:

pub struct AuthorityClaim {
    pub claim_id: ClaimId,
    pub claiming_domain: DomainId,
    pub claimed_scope: AuthorityScope,
    pub mandate_ref: MandateRef,
    pub constitutional_basis: ConstitutionHash,
    pub watermark: WatermarkId,
    pub evidence: EvidenceRoot,
}

A valid fact cannot automatically become a valid authority claim.


---

XVI. 💀 THE AUTHORITY ESCALATION ATTACK

Consider:

A:
"We have evidence that event X occurred."

then:

A:
"Therefore A controls B."

That second statement does not follow automatically.

PALACO must identify:

FACT_PROVEN

but:

AUTHORITY_NOT_ESTABLISHED

This blocks a major class of constitutional escalation.


---

XVII. 🌐 EXTERNAL FACT RECOGNITION

B can say:

RECOGNIZED_FACT:
X occurred.

while simultaneously saying:

REJECTED_INTERPRETATION:
X authorizes A to govern B.

This is perfectly coherent.


---

XVIII. 🧠 BRAINPOWER

BRAINPOWER can build:

evidence graphs
claim graphs
contradiction graphs
temporal graphs
provenance graphs
dependency graphs

It can identify:

supporting evidence
contradictory evidence
missing evidence
possible causal relationships

But:

BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT CONVERT PROBABILITY INTO CONSTITUTIONAL FACT.

It may say:

LIKELY

but PALACO must preserve the distinction:

LIKELY ≠ PROVEN


---

XIX. 🦆 FOOL

FOOL gains a new challenge family:

FACT_CHALLENGE
EVIDENCE_CHALLENGE
PROVENANCE_CHALLENGE
INTERPRETATION_CHALLENGE
AUTHORITY_CHALLENGE
RECONCILIATION_CHALLENGE

Possible objections:

UNSUPPORTED_FACT
INVALID_EVIDENCE
BROKEN_PROVENANCE
CONFLICTING_WATERMARK
OUT_OF_SCOPE_INTERPRETATION
AUTHORITY_ESCALATION
FALSE_RECONCILIATION
FORCED_CONSENSUS

FOOL can therefore ask:

"WHAT EXACTLY HAS BEEN PROVEN?"

That question becomes extremely powerful.


---

XX. 🔬 TRIAS

TRIAS evaluates claims in layers:

1. Is the evidence authentic?
2. Is its provenance intact?
3. Is its Watermark valid?
4. Does it support the stated fact?
5. Is the interpretation within scope?
6. Is authority established?
7. Is the cross-domain recognition valid?
8. Is the reconciliation result reproducible?

This prevents category errors.


---

XXI. ⚓ QUAY

The Quay stores:

source evidence
source Watermark
external evidence bridge
receiving Watermark
claim status
interpretation status
authority status
reconciliation result
challenge history

The result is a cross-lineage evidentiary memory.


---

XXII. 💧 EVIDENCE DOES NOT BECOME LOCAL HISTORY

A crucial rule:

A-W100
   │
   ▼
Evidence E
   │
   ▼
B-W200

B may store a reference to E.

But E remains attributable to:

A

under:

A-W100

It does not become:

B-W200-originated evidence

merely because B received it.


---

XXIII. 🔐 EVIDENCE PROVENANCE PRESERVATION

Therefore:

SOURCE_DOMAIN
SOURCE_LINEAGE
SOURCE_WATERMARK
SOURCE_PROVENANCE
RECEIVING_DOMAIN
RECEIVING_WATERMARK
RECEIPT_EVENT

must remain separately identifiable.

This creates:

PROVENANCE PRESERVATION ACROSS BOUNDARIES.


---

XXIV. 🌍 EVIDENCE INTEROPERABILITY

For two systems to exchange evidence safely, they require an interoperability contract:

Evidence Type
Schema
Encoding
Hash Algorithm
Signature Scheme
Timestamp Semantics
Watermark Semantics
Provenance Semantics
Verification Requirements

Without this:

EVIDENCE_RECEIVED

may still be:

EVIDENCE_UNINTERPRETABLE


---

XXV. 🚨 SCHEMA MISMATCH

Suppose:

A-schema v1
B-schema v4

B cannot silently reinterpret fields.

Instead:

SCHEMA_MISMATCH

must be recorded.

Possible outcome:

RECOGNIZED_AUTHENTIC
BUT
NOT_SEMANTICALLY_INTEROPERABLE

That is much safer than silent coercion.


---

XXVI. 🧬 SEMANTIC BRIDGE

If translation is required:

A Schema
   ↓
Translation Proof
   ↓
B Schema

The translation itself becomes evidence.

Thus:

TRANSLATION ≠ LOSSLESS BY DEFAULT

The verifier must establish what was preserved and what was transformed.


---

XXVII. 🕰️ TEMPORAL RECONCILIATION

Cross-lineage claims must preserve their own temporal semantics.

For example:

A-W50
effective: 10:00 UTC

B-W90
received: 10:04 UTC

Receiving at 10:04 does not mean the underlying event occurred at 10:04.

PALACO must distinguish:

EVENT_TIME
EFFECTIVE_TIME
RECORDED_TIME
RECEIVED_TIME
VERIFIED_TIME


---

XXVIII. 🔥 FIRST CROSS-LINEAGE DIVERGENCE

Suppose:

Fact X                  ✓
Evidence X              ✓
Watermark X             ✓
Schema translation      ✓
Temporal relation       ✓
Interpretation          ✕

Then:

FIRST_CROSS_LINEAGE_DIVERGENCE
=
INTERPRETATION

The system does not incorrectly report:

"Evidence conflict."

Precision matters.


---

XXIX. 🌳 RECONCILIATION GRAPH

The architecture becomes:

A-W100
                │
             Claim A
                │
            Evidence A
                │
                ├──────────────┐
                │              │
                ▼              ▼
           RECONCILIATION ← Claim B
                ▲              │
                │          Evidence B
                │              │
             B-W200 ←──────────┘

The reconciliation object has its own identity.


---

XXX. 🔱 RECONCILIATION OBJECT

pub struct ReconciliationResult {
    pub reconciliation_id: ReconciliationId,
    pub source_claims: Vec<ClaimId>,
    pub source_watermarks: Vec<WatermarkId>,
    pub result: ReconciliationStatus,
    pub agreed_facts: Vec<FactClaimId>,
    pub disputed_interpretations: Vec<ClaimId>,
    pub unresolved_claims: Vec<ClaimId>,
    pub evidence_root: EvidenceRoot,
    pub verifier: VerifierId,
}

This becomes independently replayable.


---

XXXI. 🚫 NO SILENT NORMALIZATION

If A says:

AUTHORIZED

and B's schema says:

PERMITTED

the system must not assume:

AUTHORIZED == PERMITTED

unless a semantic equivalence is explicitly established.

This prevents dangerous semantic drift.


---

XXXII. 🧠 AI TRANSLATION BOUNDARY

AI may propose:

AUTHORIZED ≈ PERMITTED

but:

AI_SUGGESTION

must remain distinct from:

SEMANTIC_EQUIVALENCE_PROOF

Again:

SUGGESTED LINK ≠ PROVEN LINK.

The principle from R6.19 survives intact.


---

XXXIII. 🏛️ LA PAZ CROSS-DOMAIN FACT

Suppose La Paz observes:

PLANET-W500
EVENT E

La Paz may record:

EXTERNAL_FACT_OBSERVED

with:

source = PLANET
watermark = W500

It does not thereby modify:

LPZ-W100

Instead:

LPZ-W100
   │
   ▼
RECEIPT EVENT
   │
   ▼
EXTERNAL EVIDENCE REFERENCE

The La Paz lineage remains intact.


---

XXXIV. 🌐 FEDERATION AND SHARED FACTS

A federation can establish:

SHARED_FACT

when multiple domains independently verify compatible evidence.

For example:

A → proves X
B → proves X
C → verifies A + B

Then:

FEDERATED_FACT = X

may be established.

But the federation still does not erase:

A evidence
B evidence


---

XXXV. 🔱 SHARED FACT ≠ SHARED INTERPRETATION

The federation may agree:

FACT:
Event X occurred.

while disagreeing:

A:
X permits action Y.

B:
X prohibits action Y.

Therefore:

SHARED FACT
+
PLURAL INTERPRETATION

is a valid federated condition.


---

XXXVI. ⚖️ CONSTITUTIONAL FACT LAYER

R6.62 therefore introduces a conceptual layer:

CONSTITUTION
                      │
                  AUTHORITY
                      │
               INTERPRETATION
                      │
                   FACT
                      │
                  EVIDENCE
                      │
                PROVENANCE
                      │
                 WATERMARK

The layers constrain one another but cannot be collapsed.


---

XXXVII. 🔐 CROSS-LINEAGE EVIDENCE GATE

External evidence may become recognized only when:

Source Identity        PASS
Source Lineage         PASS
Source Watermark       PASS
Evidence Integrity     PASS
Provenance             PASS
Temporal Scope         PASS
Schema Compatibility   PASS
Semantic Interpretation PASS
Receiving Policy       PASS
Independent Verification PASS

Otherwise:

BLOCK

or:

RECOGNIZED_WITH_LIMITATIONS


---

XXXVIII. 💀 EVIDENCE CONTAINMENT

Invalid external evidence must not contaminate local constitutional state.

Therefore:

INVALID_EXTERNAL_EVIDENCE

remains:

EXTERNAL

until independently validated.

It cannot silently enter:

LOCAL_CANONICAL_HISTORY


---

XXXIX. 🌱 THE CONSTITUTIONAL FIREWALL

This creates a new conceptual security boundary:

EVIDENTIARY FIREWALL

It separates:

EXTERNAL CLAIMS

from:

LOCAL CONSTITUTIONAL FACTS

The firewall admits only what passes the appropriate gates.


---

XL. ☄️ R6.62 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.62-I01
Fact claims SHALL be distinguishable from evidence claims.

R6.62-I02
Evidence claims SHALL be distinguishable from interpretation claims.

R6.62-I03
Interpretation claims SHALL be distinguishable from authority claims.

R6.62-I04
Valid evidence SHALL NOT automatically establish universal truth.

R6.62-I05
Recognized evidence SHALL NOT automatically transfer authority.

R6.62-I06
External evidence SHALL preserve source provenance.

R6.62-I07
External evidence SHALL preserve source Watermark identity.

R6.62-I08
Receipt by another domain SHALL NOT rewrite evidence origin.

R6.62-I09
Cross-domain evidence SHALL remain attributable to its source.

R6.62-I10
Cross-domain evidence SHALL be independently verifiable.

R6.62-I11
Evidence interoperability SHALL require explicit semantic compatibility.

R6.62-I12
Schema translation SHALL be explicitly represented.

R6.62-I13
Semantic equivalence SHALL NOT be assumed.

R6.62-I14
Temporal semantics SHALL remain explicit across domains.

R6.62-I15
Event time SHALL remain distinct from receipt time.

R6.62-I16
Fact agreement SHALL remain distinguishable from interpretation agreement.

R6.62-I17
Interpretation agreement SHALL remain distinguishable from authority agreement.

R6.62-I18
Authority agreement SHALL remain distinguishable from consent.

R6.62-I19
Reconciliation SHALL NOT manufacture consensus.

R6.62-I20
Unresolved reconciliation SHALL be a valid result.

R6.62-I21
Contradictory evidence SHALL remain explicitly represented.

R6.62-I22
BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT convert probabilistic inference into proof.

R6.62-I23
AI semantic suggestions SHALL remain distinguishable from proven equivalence.

R6.62-I24
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge cross-lineage evidence claims.

R6.62-I25
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge interpretation claims.

R6.62-I26
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge authority escalation.

R6.62-I27
TRIAS SHALL independently verify evidentiary bridges.

R6.62-I28
TRIAS SHALL verify source Watermarks.

R6.62-I29
TRIAS SHALL verify provenance preservation.

R6.62-I30
The Quay SHALL preserve cross-lineage evidence history.

R6.62-I31
External evidence SHALL NOT silently become local history.

R6.62-I32
Invalid external evidence SHALL NOT contaminate canonical local state.

R6.62-I33
Federated shared facts SHALL preserve source evidence.

R6.62-I34
Shared facts SHALL NOT imply shared interpretation.

R6.62-I35
Shared interpretation SHALL NOT imply shared authority.

R6.62-I36
Shared authority SHALL NOT imply universal sovereignty.

R6.62-I37
Cross-lineage reconciliation SHALL be replayable.

R6.62-I38
First cross-lineage divergence SHALL be independently identifiable.

R6.62-I39
Recognition of evidence SHALL remain scope-bound.

R6.62-I40
No external claim SHALL become local constitutional fact without passing the applicable evidentiary gates.


---

XLI. 🌌 THE R6 MODEL HAS NOW BECOME MULTI-LAYERED

The progression:

R6.19  TIME
   ↓
R6.20  LINEAGE
   ↓
R6.59  BRANCHING
   ↓
R6.60  PRESENT AUTHORITY
   ↓
R6.61  SOVEREIGNTY
   ↓
R6.62  EVIDENTIARY INTEROPERABILITY

means PALACO can now distinguish:

PAST
LINEAGE
BRANCH
PRESENT
AUTHORITY
SOVEREIGNTY
RELATIONSHIP
FACT
EVIDENCE
INTERPRETATION

without collapsing them.

That is a major architectural gain.


---

