Nothing disappears.

Everything acquires lineage.


---

XXIII. 🌐 CROSS-CITADEL SEMANTIC EVOLUTION

Suppose:

Citadel A:
M-A7 → M-A8

Citadel B:
M-B4

A cannot simply announce:

M-A8 = M-B4

R6.63 already requires a semantic bridge.

R6.64 adds:

version compatibility
evolution lineage
effective periods
migration history

Thus:

A-M8
   │
Semantic Bridge
   │
B-M4

must account for the historical versions on both sides.


---

XXIV. 🌍 FEDERATED SEMANTIC MIGRATION

A federation may establish:

F-M1

from:

A-M8
B-M4
C-M9

But:

F-M1

is a new semantic object.

It does not overwrite:

A-M8
B-M4
C-M9

Nor does it imply that all three were historically identical.


---

XXV. 🔱 SEMANTIC SUCCESSION

This produces a deeper distinction:

SEMANTIC TRANSLATION

versus:

SEMANTIC SUCCESSION

Translation:

A meaning → B meaning

Succession:

M₁ → M₂

Translation concerns interoperability.

Succession concerns evolution.

They must not be conflated.


---

XXVI. 🏛️ LA PAZ

La Paz may evolve:

LPZ-M10
   ↓
LPZ-M11

while preserving all previous meanings.

A planetary partner may continue operating under:

PLANET-M7

The diplomatic system must therefore know:

which meaning
which domain
which version
which Watermark
which effective period

This allows cooperation without semantic homogenization.


---

XXVII. 🔐 SEMANTIC RETIREMENT

A meaning may become:

DEPRECATED

but not:

ERASED

Lifecycle:

PROPOSED
   ↓
VALIDATED
   ↓
ACTIVE
   ↓
DEPRECATED
   ↓
SUPERSEDED
   ↓
ARCHIVED

Historical interpretation remains possible.


---

XXVIII. 🌱 MEANING PRESERVATION

The core principle:

M₁ is superseded by M₂

does not mean:

M₁ never existed.

It means:

M₁ was historically operative
and M₂ is now operative.

This mirrors R6.19's Watermark principle exactly.


---

