XXXIV. 🧠 AI AND SEMANTIC EVOLUTION

AI may discover:

semantic drift
definition conflicts
historical inconsistencies
migration candidates
compatibility risks

But AI cannot silently rewrite:

M₁

into:

M₂

The transformation requires an explicit constitutional event.

Therefore:

AI MAY DISCOVER DRIFT. IT MAY NOT HIDE DRIFT.


---

XXXV. 🦆 FOOL AS HISTORICAL GUARDIAN

FOOL now has a particularly important role:

"What did this word mean then?"

versus:

"What does this word mean now?"

If the answer differs:

SEMANTIC_DRIFT

must be visible.

FOOL protects the historical distinction.


---

XXXVI. 🔱 THE NO-RETROACTIVE-LIE PRINCIPLE

R6.64 canonizes:

> A system SHALL NOT retroactively assign a later semantic definition to an earlier constitutional event merely because the later definition is more convenient, more precise, or currently canonical.



Or:

TODAY'S MEANING CANNOT ERASE YESTERDAY'S MEANING.


---

