R6.65 makes canonical:

> A constitutional successor SHALL inherit history by proof, not by declaration. A new generation may transform its predecessor's constitution, semantics, rules, schemas, authority structures, and implementation, but every material transformation SHALL remain attributable to an explicit and independently verifiable succession event.



Or:

