R6.64 said:

> Meaning may evolve, but its evolution requires lineage.



R6.65 now generalizes all four:

CONSTITUTIONAL GENERATIONS ARE HISTORICAL OBJECTS.

A new generation does not simply replace the old.

It says:

I came from here.
This was the final state.
These were the rules.
These were the meanings.
These authorities existed.
These protections were inherited.
These things changed.
These things were retired.
These things were added.
