I. 🌌 THE BRANCHING PROBLEM

A constitutional generation can legitimately evolve in different directions:

G₀
                /  \
               /    \
             G₁      G₂
              │       │
             W₁      W₂

Both may be valid.

This creates a fundamental distinction:

VALIDITY
   ≠
UNIQUENESS

The fact that G₁ exists does not automatically invalidate G₂.

Likewise:

MAJORITY
   ≠
PROOF

and:

POPULARITY
   ≠
CONSTITUTIONAL LEGITIMACY


