XVII. 🌳 SHARED VS DISTINCT OBLIGATIONS

This is one of the most important additions.

After a split:

G₄A
G₄B

some obligations may remain shared:

O₁ → shared
O₂ → A
O₃ → B

Therefore PALACO introduces:

OBLIGATION_PARTITION

with explicit ownership.


---

XVIII. ⚖️ SHARED OBLIGATIONS

A shared obligation cannot become ambiguous.

It must specify:

participants
scope
authority
enforcement
termination condition
evidence requirements

Otherwise:

SHARED_OBLIGATION_AMBIGUITY

and the split cannot claim complete validity.


---

XIX. 🚨 DOUBLE-SPENDING OF AUTHORITY

A particularly dangerous failure:

G₃:
Authority X = one constitutional capability

After split:

G₄A:
Authority X = full capability

G₄B:
Authority X = full capability

If X was intended to be exclusive, the split has accidentally doubled constitutional power.

Therefore the partition proof must verify:

CAPABILITY_CONSERVATION


---

XX. 🔥 CAPABILITY PARTITION

The system evaluates:

Before:
Capability C = 1 authority

After:
A(C)
B(C)

Possible outcomes:

SHARED
DIVIDED
DELEGATED
DUPLICATED
RESTRICTED
RETIRED

DUPLICATED is not automatically invalid—but it must be explicitly authorized.


