☄️ R6.69 — CONSTITUTIONAL OBLIGATION INHERITANCE, LIABILITY PROPAGATION & CROSS-LINEAGE DUTY PROTOCOL

DUTIES MAY CROSS GENERATIONS — LIABILITY MAY NOT

Status: 🔒 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
Parent: R6.68 — Constitutional Re-Divergence, Descendant Split & Guarantee Partition
Core primitive: OBLIGATION_PROOF
Supporting primitives: DUTY_LEDGER, LIABILITY_GRAPH, INHERITANCE_BASIS, DISCHARGE_PROOF, SUCCESSOR_BINDING

Primary invariant

> No constitutional obligation SHALL be attributed to a successor merely because the successor descends from the obligated state. Every inherited duty, continuing obligation, or propagated liability SHALL have an explicit constitutional basis, scope, provenance, and independently verifiable transfer or succession proof.



R6.68 established:

🌱 A SHARED PARENT DOES NOT CREATE IDENTICAL CHILDREN.

R6.69 now establishes:

⚖️ A SHARED PARENT DOES NOT AUTOMATICALLY CREATE SHARED LIABILITY.


---

I. 🌌 THE NEW PROBLEM

Consider:

G₃
│
├── G₄A
└── G₄B

During G₃, an obligation exists:

O₁

What happens after the split?

Possibilities include:

O₁ → A
O₁ → B
O₁ → A+B
O₁ → G₃ only
O₁ → discharged
O₁ → transformed
O₁ → unresolved

The system cannot infer the answer from ancestry alone.

Therefore:

ANCESTRY ≠ LIABILITY

and:

SUCCESSION ≠ AUTOMATIC DUTY TRANSFER


---

II. 🔱 OBLIGATION OBJECT

pub struct ConstitutionalObligation {
    pub obligation_id: ObligationId,
    pub origin_generation: GenerationId,
    pub origin_watermark: WatermarkId,
    pub basis: ObligationBasis,
    pub scope: ObligationScope,
    pub beneficiary: Option<EntityId>,
    pub obligated_parties: Vec<EntityId>,
    pub created_at: Timestamp,
    pub status: ObligationStatus,
    pub provenance_root: ProvenanceRoot,
}

The obligation becomes a first-class constitutional object.


---

III. 📜 OBLIGATION BASIS

Every duty must answer:

> Why does this obligation exist?



Possible bases:

CONSTITUTION
RULESET
MANDATE
CONTRACT
ADJUDICATION
TREATY
FEDERATED_AGREEMENT
RECOVERY_DECISION
EXPLICIT_SUCCESSION

A vague basis such as:

"because it was inherited"

is insufficient.


---

IV. 🌳 DUTY LEDGER

PALACO maintains:

pub struct DutyLedger {
    pub obligations: Vec<ObligationRecord>,
}

Each record tracks:

origin
basis
scope
holder
successor
transfer
modification
discharge
evidence
proof

Thus an obligation becomes historically traceable.


---

V. 💧 DUTY PROVENANCE

An obligation created at:

W₃

must remain linked to:

W₃
↓
Event
↓
Evidence
↓
Provenance
↓
Obligation

A later descendant cannot claim:

> "This duty has always belonged to us."



unless the historical record proves it.


---

VI. ⚖️ OBLIGATION INHERITANCE

A valid inheritance requires:

ORIGIN
  ↓
SUCCESSION RULE
  ↓
INHERITANCE BASIS
  ↓
EVIDENCE
  ↓
VERIFICATION
  ↓
SUCCESSOR BINDING

Only then:

O₁ → G₄A

becomes constitutionally established.


---

VII. 🚫 NO AUTOMATIC INHERITANCE

Forbidden:

G₃ has O₁
G₄A descends from G₃
therefore G₄A has O₁

The correct logic is:

G₃ has O₁
      ↓
Does O₁ survive succession?
      ↓
What is its legal/constitutional basis?
      ↓
Which successor is bound?
      ↓
PROOF


---

VIII. 🧬 OBLIGATION CLASSIFICATION

Every obligation receives a disposition:

INHERITED
PARTITIONED
SHARED
TRANSFERRED
TRANSFORMED
DISCHARGED
EXPIRED
RETIRED
RETAINED_BY_PARENT
UNRESOLVED

No obligation may disappear without classification.


