XIV. 🚨 NO LIABILITY BY BLOODLINE

Canonical principle:

> A descendant SHALL NOT inherit liability solely because it is genealogically or constitutionally descended from the responsible predecessor.



Instead:

G₃ liable
↓
Does successor law transfer liability?
↓
Does successor entity assume the relevant obligation?
↓
Is the liability transferable?
↓
Evidence
↓
Proof


---

XV. 🧠 BRAINPOWER

BRAINPOWER may identify:

possible successor obligation
possible liability dependency
possible assumption
possible discharge
possible partition

It may produce:

OBLIGATION_TRANSFER_CANDIDATE
LIABILITY_PROPAGATION_CANDIDATE

But never:

AUTOMATIC_SUCCESSOR_LIABILITY


---

XVI. 🦆 FOOL

FOOL gains:

OBLIGATION_CHALLENGE
LIABILITY_CHALLENGE

Possible grounds:

NO_BASIS
WRONG_SUCCESSOR
SCOPE_EXPANSION
RETROACTIVE_ASSIGNMENT
MISSING_EVIDENCE
BROKEN_PROVENANCE
UNAUTHORIZED_TRANSFER
DUPLICATED_DUTY
FALSE_LIABILITY

FOOL can ask:

"Show me the constitutional bridge between the original obligation and this successor."


---

XVII. 🔬 TRIAS

TRIAS verifies:

obligation identity
origin
basis
scope
provenance
successor relationship
transfer event
evidence
adjudication
liability basis
discharge
replay

TRIAS cannot create a missing bridge.


---

XVIII. ⚓ QUAY

The Quay preserves the complete obligation history:

G₃
 │
 ├── O₁ CREATED
 │
 ├── O₁ CHALLENGED
 │
 ├── O₁ ADJUDICATED
 │
 ├── O₁ TRANSFERRED
 │
 └── G₄A
       │
       └── O₁ ACTIVE

Every transition remains append-only.


---

XIX. 🌳 PARTITIONED DUTY

An obligation can split:

O₁
│
├── O₁A → G₄A
└── O₁B → G₄B

But the partition itself must be proven.

Example:

O₁ = preserve 100% archive

could become:

A = preserve records 1–50
B = preserve records 51–100

This is:

DUTY_PARTITION

not ordinary inheritance.


---

XX. 🔱 SHARED DUTY

Alternatively:

O₁
│
├── G₄A
└── G₄B

both remain responsible.

Then PALACO must specify:

joint responsibility
individual responsibility
coordination duty
failure condition
evidence obligation

Otherwise:

SHARED_DUTY_AMBIGUITY

blocks activation.


---

XXI. 🚫 DUTY DUPLICATION

A dangerous split:

O₁ = exclusive authority obligation

becomes:

G₄A → O₁
G₄B → O₁

If exclusivity was part of the original obligation, this creates an invalid duplication.

Therefore:

DUTY CONSERVATION MUST BE PROVEN.


---

XXII. 🧬 LIABILITY PROPAGATION

Possible graph:

G₃
 │
 ├── breach E₁
 │      ↓
 │   liability L₁
 │
 └── split
       / \
      A   B

The system must determine:

L₁ → A
L₁ → B
L₁ → A+B
L₁ → G₃
L₁ → discharged

based on evidence and constitutional basis.


---

XXIII. 🕰️ NO RETROACTIVE LIABILITY

Forbidden:

G₄A created at T₂
       ↓
liability assigned
       ↓
based solely on event at T₁

unless a valid constitutional rule explicitly establishes successor responsibility.

Temporal provenance is mandatory.


---

XXIV. 💧 LIABILITY WATERMARK

Every material liability state receives historical anchoring:

L₁
 ↓
W₃
 ↓
Adjudication
 ↓
W₄A

The verifier can therefore answer:

> When did this liability exist, under which constitution, and why was it attributed to this entity?




---

XXV. 🌐 CROSS-LINEAGE DUTIES

Two branches may share an obligation:

G₄A ─────┐
         │
       O_SHARED
         │
G₄B ─────┘

This creates a cross-lineage relationship.

It must itself have:

CrossLineageAgreement
Scope
Authority
Evidence
Termination
Watermark

The relationship cannot exist merely because the branches share an ancestor.


---

XXVI. 🏛️ FEDERATED DUTIES

A federation may establish:

F₁:
cross-domain evidence preservation

which binds:

A
B
C

A local split later occurs:

A → A₁ + A₂

The system must explicitly determine whether:

A₁
A₂

remain bound to the federated duty.

Again:

FEDERATED ANCESTRY ≠ AUTOMATIC FEDERATED LIABILITY


---

XXVII. 🌱 LA PAZ

For La Paz:

LPZ-G₃
 │
 ├── LPZ-A
 └── LPZ-B

a diplomatic obligation may be:

LPZ-G₃:
honor treaty T

After division:

LPZ-A → treaty T
LPZ-B → treaty T

only if the succession framework proves that the treaty obligation survives and applies to both.

Otherwise:

T → unresolved

and the system must not pretend otherwise.


---

XXVIII. 🔬 REPLAY

The Proof Machine reconstructs:

Replay(
    SourceWatermark,
    ObligationEvents,
    SuccessionRules,
    PartitionRules,
    Adjudications
)
→ DutyState

Then:

ExpectedDutyState == ReplayedDutyState

must hold.

For liability:

ExpectedLiabilityState == ReplayedLiabilityState

must also hold.


---

XXIX. 🚨 FIRST DUTY DIVERGENCE

Example:

Origin ✓
Obligation ✓
Succession ✓
Partition ✓
A-binding ✓
B-binding ✕

Then:

FIRST_DUTY_DIVERGENCE = B_BINDING

This makes the failure forensically precise.


---

XXX. 🔐 DISCHARGE PROOF

An obligation cannot simply vanish.

It must reach:

FULFILLED
DISCHARGED
EXPIRED
REVOKED
SUPERSEDED
ADJUDICATED

with evidence.

Thus:

O₁
 ↓
DISCHARGE EVENT
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
PROOF
 ↓
O₁ = DISCHARGED


---

XXXI. 💀 FALSE DISCHARGE

A particularly serious failure:

O₁
 ↓
"discharged"

without:

evidence
authority
basis

becomes:

FABRICATED_DISCHARGE

The obligation remains:

UNPROVEN

rather than disappearing.


---

XXXII. 🧠 BRAINPOWER + 🦆 FOOL + 🔬 TRIAS

The constitutional triad becomes:

BRAINPOWER
   ↓
find possible inheritance

FOOL
   ↓
challenge attribution

TRIAS
   ↓
prove or reject attribution

This keeps discovery separate from constitutional authority.


---

XXXIII. 🔱 SUCCESSOR BINDING

A successor binding must contain:

source obligation
successor
binding basis
scope
effective event
evidence
verification

Conceptually:

pub struct SuccessorBinding {
    pub obligation_id: ObligationId,
    pub successor: GenerationId,
    pub basis: InheritanceBasis,
    pub effective_event: EventId,
    pub proof: ProofId,
}


---

XXXIV. 🌌 OBLIGATION DAG

PALACO now supports:

O₀
             /    \
           O₁      O₂
            \      /
             O₃
             |
        partition
          /   \
        O₄A   O₄B

This means obligations themselves possess constitutional lineage.

The system can distinguish:

STATE LINEAGE
OBLIGATION LINEAGE
LIABILITY LINEAGE

without confusing them.


---

XXXV. 🔥 THE THREE-LINEAGE RULE

R6.69 introduces:

STATE LINEAGE
      +
DUTY LINEAGE
      +
LIABILITY LINEAGE

They may correlate.

They are not identical.

Therefore:

A STATE'S DESCENDANT IS NOT NECESSARILY THE DESCENDANT OF EVERY DUTY OR LIABILITY OF THAT STATE.

That distinction is architecturally enormous.


---

XXXVI. 💧 PROVENANCE COMPOSITION

A valid successor liability may therefore require:

StateLineageProof
        +
ObligationLineageProof
        +
LiabilityOriginProof
        +
SuccessionBindingProof

which compose into:

SUCCESSOR_LIABILITY_PROOF


---

XXXVII. 🚨 LIABILITY GATE

A successor may not be marked liable unless:

Origin Event              PASS
Duty Basis                PASS
Breach Evidence           PASS
Liability Adjudication    PASS
Successor Relationship    PASS
Transfer Basis             PASS
Temporal Validity         PASS
Provenance                 PASS
Independent Verification  PASS
Replay                     PASS

Otherwise:

LIABILITY_UNPROVEN

—not liable by default.


---

XXXVIII. 🔒 R6.69 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.69-I01
Every constitutional obligation SHALL have an identifiable origin.

R6.69-I02
Every obligation SHALL have an explicit constitutional basis.

R6.69-I03
Every obligation SHALL be provenance-bound.

R6.69-I04
Obligation inheritance SHALL NOT be inferred solely from ancestry.

R6.69-I05
Every inherited obligation SHALL possess an inheritance basis.

R6.69-I06
Every inherited obligation SHALL identify its successor.

R6.69-I07
Every transferred obligation SHALL have an explicit transfer event.

R6.69-I08
Every partitioned obligation SHALL identify its resulting duties.

R6.69-I09
Every shared obligation SHALL identify all participating successors.

R6.69-I10
Shared obligations SHALL define scope and responsibility.

R6.69-I11
No obligation SHALL disappear without an explicit disposition.

R6.69-I12
Every discharged obligation SHALL have discharge evidence.

R6.69-I13
A false or unsupported discharge SHALL NOT terminate an obligation.

R6.69-I14
Liability SHALL remain distinct from duty.

R6.69-I15
Liability SHALL have an identifiable originating event.

R6.69-I16
Liability SHALL have an identifiable basis.

R6.69-I17
Liability SHALL NOT be assigned solely through ancestry.

R6.69-I18
Successor liability SHALL require an explicit constitutional bridge.

R6.69-I19
Retroactive liability SHALL NOT be fabricated.

R6.69-I20
BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT autonomously assign successor liability.

R6.69-I21
AI-generated inheritance candidates SHALL remain provisional.

R6.69-I22
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge obligation inheritance.

R6.69-I23
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge liability propagation.

R6.69-I24
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge discharge claims.

R6.69-I25
TRIAS SHALL independently verify obligation inheritance.

R6.69-I26
TRIAS SHALL independently verify liability propagation.

R6.69-I27
TRIAS SHALL NOT silently repair missing inheritance evidence.

R6.69-I28
The Quay SHALL preserve obligation and liability histories.

R6.69-I29
Obligation transitions SHALL be replayable.

R6.69-I30
Liability transitions SHALL be replayable.

R6.69-I31
First duty divergence SHALL be independently identifiable.

R6.69-I32
First liability divergence SHALL be independently identifiable.

R6.69-I33
Historical obligations SHALL remain auditable after successor activation.

R6.69-I34
Historical liability records SHALL remain immutable.

R6.69-I35
Cross-lineage duties SHALL require explicit agreement or constitutional basis.

R6.69-I36
Federated duties SHALL define successor applicability explicitly.

R6.69-I37
State lineage SHALL remain distinct from obligation lineage.

R6.69-I38
Obligation lineage SHALL remain distinct from liability lineage.

R6.69-I39
No successor SHALL claim complete assumption where material transfer evidence is absent.

R6.69-I40
No constitutional liability SHALL become ACTIVE without independently verifiable attribution proof.


---

XXXIX. ☄️ THE R6 ACCOUNTABILITY GRAPH

R6 now expands into:

CONSTITUTION
      ↓
RULESET
      ↓
MANDATE
      ↓
ACTION
      ↓
EVIDENCE
      ↓
PROVENANCE
      ↓
EVENT
      ↓
QUAY
      ↓
WATERMARK
      ↓
LINEAGE
      ↓
SUCCESSION
      ↓
CONVERGENCE / DIVERGENCE
      ↓
OBLIGATION
      ↓
DUTY PARTITION
      ↓
BREACH
      ↓
LIABILITY
      ↓
SUCCESSOR ATTRIBUTION
      ↓
PROOF

The important realization is now:

PALACO DOES NOT ONLY TRACE STATES.

It traces the normative consequences of states.


---

XL. 🌳 THE DEEP PRINCIPLE

A constitutional machine must know not merely:

> "Who came after whom?"



but:

> "Which duties came after which duties, why did they survive, and who can legitimately be held accountable for them?"



That is the beginning of genuine constitutional accountability across generations.


---

XLI. ⚖️ THE LIABILITY PRINCIPLE

R6.69 therefore makes canonical:

> A successor may inherit an obligation only where the inheritance is constitutionally grounded and proven. Liability may propagate only where its attribution to the successor is independently established. Ancestry alone SHALL never constitute sufficient proof of liability.



Or:

🌱 SUCCESSION DOES NOT EQUAL ASSUMPTION.

⚖️ DUTY DOES NOT EQUAL LIABILITY.

💧 LIABILITY DOES NOT EXIST WITHOUT PROVENANCE.

🔬 ATTRIBUTION MUST BE PROVEN.


---

XLII. 🔒 R6.69 SEALED

The constitutional lineage engine now possesses three distinct but composable histories:

CONSTITUTIONAL STATE
                         │
                    STATE LINEAGE
                         │
              ┌──────────┴──────────┐
              ▼                     ▼
        OBLIGATION LINEAGE     AUTHORITY LINEAGE
              │
              ▼
         DUTY / BREACH
              │
              ▼
       LIABILITY LINEAGE

This is a major architectural boundary.

Because the next unavoidable question is no longer simply who inherits a duty.

It is:

> What happens when the very identity of the constitutional actor changes—when an entity is replaced, merged, split, dissolved, delegated, or reborn—and PALACO must prove whether the actor itself remains the same constitutional subject?



That opens:

☄️ R6.70 — CONSTITUTIONAL IDENTITY, ENTITY CONTINUITY & SUBJECT SUCCESSION PROTOCOL

ENTITY A
   │
   ├── identity proof
   ├── authority proof
   ├── obligation proof
   └── lineage proof
          │
          ▼
     TRANSFORMATION
          │
     ┌────┴────┐
     ▼         ▼
   ENTITY B  ENTITY C

The hard principle:

🔱 A NEW NAME IS NOT NECESSARILY A NEW ENTITY.

And equally:

💀 A NEW ENTITY IS NOT NECESSARILY THE OLD ENTITY WITH A NEW NAME.

PALACO will need to prove the difference.

☄️🌱🦆💧⚓🔬🧠🔱🏛️❤️

R6.69 — SEALED.

☄️ R6.70 — CONSTITUTIONAL IDENTITY, ENTITY CONTINUITY & SUBJECT SUCCESSION PROTOCOL

IDENTITY MUST BE PROVEN — NOT INFERRED FROM A NAME

Status: 🔒 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
Parent: R6.69 — Constitutional Obligation Inheritance, Liability Propagation & Cross-Lineage Duty Protocol
Core primitive: IDENTITY_PROOF
Supporting primitives: SUBJECT_ID, IDENTITY_CLAIM, IDENTITY_TRANSITION, AUTHORITY_CONTINUITY, DUTY_CONTINUITY, ENTITY_WATERMARK

Primary invariant

> No constitutional actor SHALL be treated as the same subject, successor, replacement, or continuation of another actor without an independently verifiable identity-transition proof.



R6.69 established:

⚖️ SUCCESSION DOES NOT EQUAL ASSUMPTION.

R6.70 establishes:

🔱 SUCCESSION DOES NOT EQUAL IDENTITY.


---

I. 🌌 THE IDENTITY PROBLEM

Consider:

ENTITY A
   ↓
rename
   ↓
ENTITY B

Is B still A?

Possibly.

Now:

ENTITY A
   ↓
dissolution
   ↓
ENTITY B

Is B A?

Possibly not.

And:

ENTITY A + ENTITY B
        ↓
      ENTITY C

What happened to:

authority?

obligations?

liabilities?

provenance?

historical identity?

constitutional rights?

permissions?


A name cannot answer these questions.

Therefore:

IDENTITY IS A PROVABLE CONSTITUTIONAL PROPERTY.


---

II. 🔱 SUBJECT IDENTITY

pub struct SubjectIdentity {
    pub subject_id: SubjectId,
    pub identity_root: IdentityRoot,
    pub inception_watermark: WatermarkId,
    pub current_status: SubjectStatus,
    pub authority_root: AuthorityRoot,
    pub provenance_root: ProvenanceRoot,
}

The SubjectId is therefore not merely:

name
hostname
UUID
account

It represents a constitutionally recognized actor.


---

III. 💧 IDENTITY ROOT

The identity root binds:

SUBJECT
+
ORIGIN
+
CONSTITUTIONAL BASIS
+
AUTHORITY
+
PROVENANCE

Conceptually:

IdentityRoot =
H(
    SubjectId
    +
OriginProof
    +
AuthorityRoot
    +
ProvenanceRoot
)

A rename therefore does not automatically generate a new identity root.


---

IV. 🧬 IDENTITY CLAIM

An identity relationship is explicitly represented:

pub struct IdentityClaim {
    pub claim_id: IdentityClaimId,
    pub source_subject: SubjectId,
    pub target_subject: SubjectId,
    pub relation: IdentityRelation,
    pub evidence: EvidenceRef,
    pub proof: ProofId,
}

Possible relations:

CONTINUATION
REPLACEMENT
SUCCESSOR
MERGER
SPLIT
DISSOLUTION
REINCORPORATION
DELEGATION
REACTIVATION
NEW_ENTITY


---

V. 🌳 IDENTITY IS NOT A LABEL

PALACO must distinguish:

NAME
IDENTIFIER
ENTITY
CONSTITUTIONAL SUBJECT

These are not interchangeable.

For example:

"Citadel Alpha"

may retain the same subject identity after:

"Citadel Prime"

is adopted.

Conversely:

"Citadel Alpha"

may be used by a completely new subject after the original entity is dissolved.

Therefore:

SAME NAME ≠ SAME SUBJECT

and:

DIFFERENT NAME ≠ DIFFERENT SUBJECT


---

VI. 🔐 IDENTITY CONTINUITY

A continuation claim requires proof of:

origin
constitutional basis
authority continuity
provenance continuity
obligation disposition
identity control
state transition

Conceptually:

A
↓
IDENTITY TRANSITION
↓
B

becomes:

A ==continuation-proof==> B

only after verification.


---

VII. 🚫 NO IMPLICIT CONTINUITY

Forbidden:

A → B

because:

same name
same operator
same database
same server
same address

Any of these may be evidence.

None is sufficient alone.


---

VIII. 🧬 ENTITY TRANSFORMATION

R6.70 models transformations explicitly:

A
 ↓
TRANSFORMATION
 ↓
B

with:

pub struct IdentityTransition {
    pub transition_id: TransitionId,
    pub source: SubjectId,
    pub targets: Vec<SubjectId>,
    pub transition_type: IdentityTransitionType,
    pub basis: TransitionBasis,
    pub evidence: Vec<EvidenceRef>,
    pub proof: ProofId,
}


---

IX. 🌱 CONTINUATION

Example:

A
 ↓
constitutional reorganization
 ↓
A'

If identity continuity is proven:

SubjectId(A) == SubjectId(A')

while:

Generation(A) != Generation(A')

This distinction is critical.

ENTITY IDENTITY MAY CONTINUE WHILE CONSTITUTIONAL STATE CHANGES.


---

X. 🔥 REPLACEMENT

Consider:

A
 ↓
retirement
 ↓
B

B may inherit:

duties
systems
assets
operational roles

without becoming:

A

Therefore:

A ≠ B

may coexist with:

A.duties → B

This connects directly to R6.69.


---

XI. ⚖️ IDENTITY ≠ OBLIGATION

This becomes a formal rule:

Identity lineage
      ≠
Obligation lineage

Thus:

A → B

does not automatically mean:

Identity(A) = Identity(B)

nor:

Obligation(A) = Obligation(B)

Each relationship requires its own proof.


---

XII. 💀 LIABILITY IDENTITY

Likewise:

A liable

does not automatically mean:

B liable

even where:

B succeeds A

R6.69 remains binding.

The system must separately establish:

successor liability


---

XIII. 🔱 MERGER IDENTITY

Suppose:

A + B
   ↓
C

There are multiple possibilities:

Model 1 — New Subject

A ─┐
   ├──→ C
B ─┘

C ≠ A
C ≠ B

Model 2 — Continuation of A

A ───→ C
B ───→ C

C continues A

Model 3 — New Federation

A ───┐
     ├──→ C
B ───┘

A and B remain independent

PALACO must not choose between these models by assumption.


---

XIV. 🌳 SPLIT IDENTITY

R6.68 already permits:

A
│
├── B
└── C

But R6.70 clarifies:

B ≠ C

even if both claim continuity from A.

Possible:

B = continuation of A in jurisdiction X
C = continuation of A in jurisdiction Y

or:

B = new entity
C = new entity

The distinction must be proven.


---

XV. 🕰️ TEMPORAL IDENTITY

Identity transitions are temporally bounded:

A ACTIVE
   ↓ T₁
TRANSITION
   ↓ T₂
B ACTIVE

The system must establish:

effective_time
transition_event
preceding_state
resulting_state

This prevents retroactive identity rewriting.


---

XVI. 💧 ENTITY WATERMARK

Every material identity state receives a Watermark relationship:

A
↓
W_A
↓
IdentityTransition
↓
B
↓
W_B

Thus the verifier can reconstruct:

> Which entity existed at which constitutional time and under which identity claim?




---

XVII. ⚓ QUAY IDENTITY MEMORY

The Quay preserves:

A CREATED
A ACTIVE
A TRANSFORMED
A RETIRED
B CREATED
B ACTIVE

Never:

A deleted
B substituted

without preserving the historical record.

The Quay becomes the:

IDENTITY MEMORY OF THE CONSTITUTIONAL MACHINE


---

XVIII. 🧠 BRAINPOWER

BRAINPOWER may compare:

authority structures
identity roots
provenance roots
operational continuity
constitutional signatures
obligation sets
historical behavior

and propose:

LIKELY_CONTINUATION
LIKELY_REPLACEMENT
LIKELY_NEW_SUBJECT

But:

LIKELY IDENTITY ≠ PROVEN IDENTITY


---

XIX. 🦆 FOOL

FOOL gains:

IDENTITY_CHALLENGE

with grounds:

FALSE_CONTINUATION
FALSE_SUCCESSION
NAME_CONFUSION
AUTHORITY_BREAK
PROVENANCE_BREAK
HIDDEN_DISSOLUTION
UNAUTHORIZED_REINCORPORATION
LIABILITY_ESCAPE
DUTY_ESCAPE
FABRICATED_IDENTITY

The strongest challenge may be:

> "Show the proof that this actor is the same constitutional subject."




---

XX. 🔬 TRIAS

TRIAS verifies:

identity root
origin
transition event
constitutional basis
authority continuity
provenance
obligation disposition
liability disposition
Watermarks
signatures
replay

TRIAS cannot infer identity from operational similarity.


---

XXI. 🔐 AUTHORITY CONTINUITY

A critical distinction:

ENTITY CONTINUITY

does not automatically imply:

AUTHORITY CONTINUITY

Example:

A:
authority X = allowed

After transformation:

B:
authority X = restricted

The entity may remain the same while its authority changes.

Thus:

IDENTITY CAN CONTINUE WHILE AUTHORITY EVOLVES.


---

XXII. 🌱 DUTY CONTINUITY

Likewise:

A
 ↓
B

may retain identity but change duties:

O₁ → retained
O₂ → discharged
O₃ → transformed

The identity proof does not substitute for obligation proofs.


---

XXIII. ⚖️ LIABILITY SHIELDING FORBIDDEN

A particularly important invariant:

A constitutional actor cannot evade a legitimately established liability merely by:

renaming
restructuring
changing schema
creating a new generation
changing deployment
moving jurisdictions

But neither may PALACO assign liability merely because such a transformation occurred.

The correct process remains:

LIABILITY BASIS
↓
IDENTITY RELATION
↓
SUCCESSOR RELATION
↓
ATTRIBUTION PROOF


---

XXIV. 💀 FALSE DISSOLUTION

A subject may attempt:

A
 ↓
"dissolved"
 ↓
B

while continuing all material authority and obligations through B.

PALACO does not automatically classify this as either:

continuation

or:

new entity

It becomes an evidence-bearing identity dispute.

IDENTITY_DISPUTE


---

XXV. 🦆 FOOL ADJUDICATION

FOOL may challenge:

A dissolved

with:

CONTINUITY_EVIDENCE
AUTHORITY_EVIDENCE
PROVENANCE_EVIDENCE
OBLIGATION_EVIDENCE

The dispute then enters the existing:

CHALLENGE
↓
ADJUDICATION
↓
PROOF
↓
WATERMARK

pipeline.


---

XXVI. 🌐 CROSS-CITADEL IDENTITY

Two Citadels may recognize an actor differently:

Citadel A:
Subject X

Citadel B:
Subject Y

PALACO cannot simply declare:

X == Y

A cross-domain identity claim requires:

IDENTITY_RECOGNITION_EVENT
+
EVIDENCE
+
PROOF

This creates:

CROSS_DOMAIN_IDENTITY_PROOF


---

XXVII. 🏛️ LA PAZ

La Paz may recognize:

LPZ-S1

while the planetary federation recognizes:

PLANET-S9

A diplomatic relationship can state:

PLANET-S9 recognizes LPZ-S1

without asserting:

PLANET-S9 == LPZ-S1

This preserves jurisdictional sovereignty and avoids accidental identity collapse.


---

XXVIII. 🔬 IDENTITY REPLAY

The Proof Machine executes:

Replay(
    IdentityOrigin,
    IdentityEvents,
    TransitionRules,
    Evidence
)
→ IdentityState

Then:

ExpectedIdentityState
==
ReplayedIdentityState

must hold.

If not:

IDENTITY_DIVERGENCE


---

XXIX. 🚨 FIRST IDENTITY DIVERGENCE

Example:

Origin ✓
A active ✓
Transition ✓
Authority mapping ✓
Provenance ✕

Then:

FIRST_IDENTITY_DIVERGENCE = PROVENANCE

rather than merely:

IDENTITY_CHECK_FAILED


---

XXX. 🔱 IDENTITY STATUS

pub enum IdentityStatus {
    Genesis,
    Active,
    Continued,
    Transformed,
    Replaced,
    Merged,
    Split,
    Dissolved,
    Reincorporated,
    Disputed,
    Unproven,
    Irrecoverable,
}

This allows PALACO to represent uncertainty explicitly.


---

XXXI. 🔥 IDENTITY GATE

A continuation claim becomes active only when:

Identity Root             PASS
Origin                    PASS
Transition Event          PASS
Constitutional Basis      PASS
Authority Analysis        PASS
Obligation Analysis       PASS
Liability Analysis        PASS
Provenance                PASS
Watermark                 PASS
Replay                    PASS
Independent Audit         PASS

Otherwise:

BLOCK


---

XXXII. 🧬 IDENTITY GRAPH

PALACO now possesses another proof-bearing graph:

A
        /   \
       /     \
      B       C
       \     /
        \   /
          D

But the edges may mean different things:

CONTINUATION
SUCCESSION
MERGER
RECOGNITION
REPLACEMENT

The graph therefore cannot be interpreted merely as ancestry.

Every edge has semantics.


---

XXXIII. 🌌 THE FOUR SEPARATIONS

R6.70 establishes four distinctions:

STATE IDENTITY
      ≠
ENTITY IDENTITY

ENTITY IDENTITY
      ≠
AUTHORITY IDENTITY

AUTHORITY IDENTITY
      ≠
OBLIGATION IDENTITY

OBLIGATION IDENTITY
      ≠
LIABILITY IDENTITY

These may correlate.

They must never be conflated.


---

XXXIV. ☄️ THE DEEP ARCHITECTURAL CONSEQUENCE

PALACO can now answer four different questions:

1. State

> What constitutional state exists?



2. Entity

> Who is the constitutional subject?



3. Authority

> What is that subject permitted to do?



4. Responsibility

> What duties and liabilities attach to that subject?



This separation prevents an enormous class of governance errors.


---

XXXV. 🔒 R6.70 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.70-I01
Every constitutional subject SHALL possess a unique SubjectId.

R6.70-I02
Every subject identity SHALL have an identifiable origin.

R6.70-I03
Every material identity transition SHALL be explicitly recorded.

R6.70-I04
Identity continuity SHALL require independent proof.

