XXXVII. 💧 THE IDENTITY PRINCIPLE

R6.70 makes canonical:

> A constitutional subject SHALL NOT be presumed continuous merely because a successor bears its name, operates its infrastructure, possesses its authority, or follows its history. Identity continuity SHALL be an explicit, evidence-bearing, provenance-bound, independently verifiable constitutional claim.



Or:

🔱 NAME IS NOT IDENTITY.

🌱 SUCCESSION IS NOT IDENTITY.

⚖️ AUTHORITY IS NOT IDENTITY.

💧 PROVENANCE ESTABLISHES THE BRIDGE.

🔬 PROOF ESTABLISHES THE CLAIM.


