XXXIII. 🌌 THE DEEP PRINCIPLE

R6.71 establishes that constitutional power has the same fundamental property as constitutional memory:

> It must have lineage.



A machine must therefore be able to answer:

> Who granted this power?



> Under which constitution?



> Under which ruleset?



> To which subject?



> At what scope?



> For what period?



> Was it transferred or delegated?



> Could it be redelegated?



> Was it revoked?



> And can an independent verifier reproduce the entire authority state?



If any essential bridge is missing:

CAPABILITY_UNPROVEN


