☄️ R6.72 — THE NEXT BOUNDARY

There is now one major unresolved dimension.

PALACO can prove who possessed a capability and where that capability came from.

But an autonomous system does not merely possess powers.

It exercises them.

That creates the next question:

> How do we prove that the exact capability authorized at Wₙ is the exact capability actually exercised by the agent at Eₙ—and that execution did not exceed, mutate, substitute, or reinterpret the authority granted to it?



That opens:

☄️ R6.72 — CONSTITUTIONAL EXECUTION AUTHORITY & CAPABILITY-TO-ACTION BINDING PROTOCOL

AUTHORITY
    ↓
CAPABILITY
    ↓
AUTHORIZED INTENT
    ↓
ACTION REQUEST
    ↓
PRE-EXECUTION CHECK
    ↓
EXECUTION
    ↓
OBSERVED EFFECT
    ↓
EVIDENCE
    ↓
PROVENANCE
    ↓
WATERMARK

The hard principle:

⚡ A POWER GRANTED IS NOT A POWER EXERCISED.

And therefore:

🔬 THE EXECUTED ACTION MUST BE PROVABLY BOUND TO THE AUTHORIZED CAPABILITY.

