---

XXXII. 🌌 THE BIG PRINCIPLE

R6.72 makes canonical:

> A capability is not evidence of execution. An execution is not evidence of authorization. Authorization becomes constitutionally attributable only when the exact action is demonstrably bound to the valid capability, authority, mandate, ruleset, subject, and temporal state under which it was executed.



Or:

⚡ NO BINDING → NO AUTHORIZED EXECUTION.

🔬 NO EXECUTION PROOF → NO CLAIM OF CONSTITUTIONAL ACTION.


---

XXXIII. 🔒 R6.72 SEALED

The architecture has reached a new level:

WHY
         │
   CONSTITUTION
         │
        RULE
         │
       MANDATE
         │
        WHO
         │
      SUBJECT
         │
      IDENTITY
         │
        MAY
         │
