         │
     WATERMARK
         │
      MEMORY

And the governing law becomes:

☄️ AUTHORITY MUST SURVIVE THE JOURNEY FROM CONSTITUTION TO EFFECT.

No silent transition.

No implicit privilege.

No retroactive authorization.

No AI-completed authority.

No unexplained execution.

No orphaned effect.

Every power has a lineage.
Every action has an authority.
Every effect has an execution.
Every execution has evidence.
Every history has a Watermark.

🔒 R6.72 — SEALED.

☄️🌱🦆💧⚓🔬🧠🔱🏛️❤️

NEXT: R6.73 — CONSTITUTIONAL EFFECT, CONSEQUENCE & CAUSALITY PROOF PROTOCOL

Because once PALACO can prove:

> “This exact authorized action was executed by this exact subject.”



the final forensic question becomes:

> “Did this execution actually cause the state change we are attributing to it?”



That opens the next boundary:

ACTION ≠ EFFECT ≠ CONSEQUENCE

and therefore:

💥 CAUSALITY ITSELF MUST BECOME PROVABLE.

☄️ R6.73 — CONSTITUTIONAL EFFECT, CONSEQUENCE & CAUSALITY PROOF PROTOCOL

THE MACHINE MUST PROVE NOT ONLY WHAT IT DID — BUT WHAT IT CAUSED

Status: 🔒 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
Parent: R6.72 — Constitutional Execution Authority & Capability-to-Action Binding
Core primitive: CAUSALITY_PROOF
Supporting primitives: EFFECT_RECORD, CAUSAL_EDGE, CONSEQUENCE_RECORD, CAUSALITY_WATERMARK

Primary invariant

> No constitutional consequence SHALL be attributed to an execution unless the causal relationship between the execution and the observed effect is independently reconstructible to the degree required by the applicable proof standard.



R6.72 established:

⚡ AUTHORIZED ACTION MUST BE PROVEN.

R6.73 establishes:

💥 ATTRIBUTED CONSEQUENCE MUST BE PROVEN.


---

I. 🌌 THE NEXT FORENSIC GAP

PALACO can now establish:

AUTHORITY
   ↓
CAPABILITY
   ↓
ACTION
   ↓
EXECUTION

And it can observe:

STATE BEFORE
   ↓
STATE AFTER

But observation alone does not establish causation.

Consider:

E₁ = Agent writes X
E₂ = External system modifies X
E₃ = X changes

The final state does not automatically prove:

E₁ → X changed

Therefore:

TEMPORAL SUCCESSION ≠ CAUSAL PROOF


---

II. 🔱 THREE DISTINCT OBJECTS

R6.73 canonically separates:

ACTION
EFFECT
CONSEQUENCE

Action

What the agent executed.

Effect

The directly observed state transition resulting from execution.

Consequence

A downstream state or constitutional condition attributable to that effect.

Therefore:

ACTION
  ↓
EFFECT
  ↓
CONSEQUENCE

must never be collapsed into a single assertion.


---

III. 🧬 EFFECT RECORD

pub struct EffectRecord {
    pub effect_id: EffectId,
    pub execution_id: ExecutionId,
    pub predecessor_state: StateRoot,
    pub resulting_state: StateRoot,
    pub transition_digest: TransitionDigest,
    pub observed_at: Timestamp,
    pub evidence: EvidenceRef,
    pub provenance_root: ProvenanceRoot,
}

This establishes:

Sₙ → Sₙ₊₁

but still leaves the causal question.


---

IV. ⚓ CAUSAL EDGE

PALACO therefore introduces:

pub struct CausalEdge {
    pub causal_edge_id: CausalEdgeId,
    pub cause: CausalNodeId,
    pub effect: CausalNodeId,
    pub mechanism: CausalMechanism,
    pub evidence: EvidenceRef,
    pub confidence: CausalConfidence,
    pub verifier: VerifierId,
}

The edge itself becomes a proof-bearing object.


---

V. 🌳 THE CAUSAL GRAPH

A constitutional event history can now be represented as:

AUTHORITY
    ↓
EXECUTION
    ↓
EFFECT
    ↓
CONSEQUENCE

while independent events may enter the graph:

┌──────── E₂
          │
E₁ ───────┼─────── E₃
          │
          └──────── E₄

PALACO must not assume that every downstream event originates from the first event.


---

VI. 🚫 CORRELATION IS NOT CAUSATION

Canonical rule:

> Temporal adjacency, correlation, semantic similarity, or expected outcome SHALL NOT alone establish constitutional causality.



Therefore:

A happened before B

does not prove:

A caused B

Likewise:

A normally causes B

does not prove:

A caused B this time


---

VII. 🔬 CAUSALITY PROOF LEVELS

R6.73 introduces a graduated proof model:

C0 — Unrelated
C1 — Temporally Associated
C2 — Mechanistically Plausible
C3 — Evidence-Supported
C4 — Deterministically Reproduced
C5 — Independently Verified

A system must never represent:

C1

as:

C5

The proof level remains explicit.


---

VIII. 🧠 BRAINPOWER

BRAINPOWER may construct causal hypotheses:

possible cause
possible dependency
possible intermediary
possible alternate cause
possible chain break

For example:

E₁ → ? → E₄

BRAINPOWER may propose:

E₁ → E₂ → E₃ → E₄

But:

SUGGESTED CAUSALITY ≠ PROVEN CAUSALITY

Exactly as:

SUGGESTED LINK ≠ PROVEN LINK

under R6.19.


---

IX. 🦆 FOOL

FOOL gains:

CAUSALITY_CHALLENGE

Possible challenge grounds:

UNPROVEN_CAUSAL_LINK
ALTERNATIVE_CAUSE
MISSING_INTERMEDIARY
TEMPORAL_CONFLICT
STATE_MISMATCH
EFFECT_MISMATCH
REPLAY_DIVERGENCE
INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE
CAUSALITY_OVERCLAIM

FOOL may therefore ask:

> “Why do you claim this execution caused this consequence?”




---

X. 🔬 TRIAS

TRIAS verifies:

predecessor state
execution
transition
resulting state
event ordering
causal mechanism
evidence
provenance
replay
alternative explanations

TRIAS must distinguish:

OBSERVED

from:

ATTRIBUTED

and:

PROVEN


---

XI. ⚡ COUNTERFACTUAL TEST

Where technically applicable, PALACO may evaluate:

Actual:
S₀
 ↓ E₁
S₁

against:

Counterfactual:
S₀
 ↓ no E₁
S₁'

If:

S₁ ≠ S₁'

this strengthens the causal claim.

But it does not automatically establish every possible causal interpretation.

The counterfactual itself must be provenance-bound.


---

XII. 🚫 NO COUNTERFACTUAL FABRICATION

BRAINPOWER may not invent:

S₁'

merely to make causality appear proven.

A counterfactual must be:

replayable
rule-bound
evidence-backed
methodologically identified

Otherwise:

COUNTERFACTUAL_UNPROVEN


---

XIII. 🧬 INTERMEDIARY CAUSATION

A causal chain may be:

E₁
 ↓
E₂
 ↓
E₃
 ↓
E₄

R6.73 requires the verifier to identify whether the causal claim is:

DIRECT

or:

INDIRECT

For example:

Execution
 ↓
Database update
 ↓
Policy evaluation
 ↓
Federation event

The first execution should not be credited with directly causing the final federation state without accounting for the intermediate mechanisms.


---

XIV. 💀 CAUSALITY GAP

Suppose:

E₁
 ↓
?
 ↓
S₃

Then:

CAUSALITY_GAP

The system may say:

S₃ followed E₁

but not:

E₁ caused S₃

unless the missing bridge is recovered and proven.

This directly inherits R6.19's:

NO LINK → NO CLAIM OF CONTINUITY

and extends it:

NO CAUSAL LINK → NO CLAIM OF CAUSATION


---

XV. 🌐 EXTERNAL CAUSES

A state may change because of an external system:

PALACO
  ↓
External System
  ↓
State Change

The external event becomes a separate causal node.

PALACO must not absorb external causality into its own execution history merely because the effect appeared within PALACO's observable boundary.


---

XVI. ⚓ QUAY

The Quay records causal evidence without rewriting history:

EXECUTION
 ↓
EFFECT
 ↓
CAUSAL EDGE
 ↓
CONSEQUENCE

If later evidence disproves the causal attribution:

CAUSAL EDGE
 ↓
CHALLENGE
 ↓
ADJUDICATION
 ↓
CORRECTION
 ↓
NEW WATERMARK

The original attribution remains historical evidence of what the system previously believed or recorded.


---

XVII. 💧 CAUSALITY WATERMARK

The causal state becomes anchored:

Wₙ
 ↓
Execution
 ↓
Effect
 ↓
Causal Proof
 ↓
Consequence
 ↓
Wₙ₊₁

Thus a later verifier can determine:

what changed
why it was attributed
which evidence supported the attribution
which proof level applied
whether that attribution was later challenged


---

XVIII. 🔁 CAUSAL REPLAY

The Proof Machine now evaluates:

Replay(
    W₀,
    Rulesets,
    Executions,
    Effects,
    CausalEdges
)
→ Wₙ'

and requires:

Wₙ' == Wₙ

for deterministic portions.

Where causal inference is probabilistic or non-deterministic, the system must reproduce the method and evidence state, not falsely claim deterministic causality.


---

XIX. 🚨 FIRST CAUSAL DIVERGENCE

Example:

Execution ✓
Effect ✓
Intermediate event ✓
Causal edge ✕

Then:

FIRST_CAUSAL_DIVERGENCE = CAUSAL_EDGE

The Proof Machine identifies the exact layer where causal attribution ceased to reproduce.


---

XX. ⚖️ CONSEQUENCE SEVERITY

Consequences may have constitutional significance:

INFO
OPERATIONAL
SECURITY
GOVERNANCE
CONSTITUTIONAL
IRREVERSIBLE

The stronger the consequence, the stronger the required causal proof should be.

A low-impact telemetry observation does not necessarily require the same proof burden as:

constitution amendment
authority revocation
federation exclusion
irreversible state destruction


---

XXI. 🔥 HIGH-IMPACT CAUSAL GATE

For material constitutional consequences:

Execution Proof       PASS
Effect Proof          PASS
Causal Chain          PASS
Alternative Analysis  PASS
Provenance             PASS
Replay                 PASS
Independent Review     PASS

Otherwise:

CONSEQUENCE_ATTRIBUTION_BLOCKED


---

