XXIV. 🌐 FEDERATED CAUSALITY

Cross-domain causal claims require domain boundaries:

DOMAIN A
  │
  ▼
A-E₁
  │
  ▼
FEDERATED EVENT
  │
  ▼
B-E₇
  │
  ▼
DOMAIN B STATE

The federation may prove:

A-E₁ contributed to B-E₇

without claiming:

A exclusively caused B-E₇

This distinction is crucial in distributed systems.


---

XXV. 🧠 CAUSAL UNCERTAINTY

PALACO must be capable of saying:

CAUSE = UNKNOWN

or:

CAUSE = MULTIPLE

or:

CAUSE = PARTIALLY_PROVEN

without forcing a binary conclusion.

A constitutional system that cannot represent uncertainty will eventually manufacture certainty.

Therefore:

EXPLICIT UNCERTAINTY IS A SECURITY PROPERTY.


---

XXVI. 🔱 CAUSALITY STATUS

pub enum CausalityStatus {
    Unrelated,
    Associated,
    Plausible,
    Supported,
    Reproduced,
    IndependentlyVerified,
    Disputed,
    Divergent,
