XXVII. ☄️ R6.73 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.73-I01
Action SHALL remain distinct from effect.

R6.73-I02
Effect SHALL remain distinct from consequence.

R6.73-I03
Temporal succession SHALL NOT alone establish causality.

R6.73-I04
Correlation SHALL NOT alone establish constitutional causality.

R6.73-I05
Every material causal claim SHALL identify its causal basis.

R6.73-I06
Every causal edge SHALL be provenance-bound.

R6.73-I07
Causal attribution SHALL identify the relevant execution or event.

R6.73-I08
Observed state change SHALL NOT automatically be attributed to the nearest preceding execution.

R6.73-I09
Alternative causal explanations SHALL remain representable.

R6.73-I10
Missing causal links SHALL remain explicitly represented.

R6.73-I11
BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT fabricate causal links.

R6.73-I12
BRAINPOWER-generated causal hypotheses SHALL remain provisional.

R6.73-I13
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge causal attribution.

R6.73-I14
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge causal sufficiency.

R6.73-I15
TRIAS SHALL independently evaluate material causal claims.

R6.73-I16
TRIAS SHALL NOT silently repair causal gaps.

R6.73-I17
Counterfactual analysis SHALL be provenance-bound where used.

R6.73-I18
Counterfactual models SHALL NOT be represented as observed history.

R6.73-I19
Indirect causality SHALL identify material intermediary events.

R6.73-I20
External causes SHALL remain distinguishable from PALACO executions.

R6.73-I21
Causal confidence SHALL remain distinct from factual observation.

R6.73-I22
Causal proof level SHALL be explicitly represented.

R6.73-I23
High-impact constitutional consequences SHALL require elevated causal proof.

R6.73-I24
Causal corrections SHALL append history rather than erase prior records.

R6.73-I25
Causal corrections SHALL receive new evidence and provenance.

R6.73-I26
Causal state SHALL be Watermark-bound.

R6.73-I27
Deterministic causal reconstruction SHALL be replayable where technically possible.

R6.73-I28
First causal divergence SHALL be independently identifiable.

R6.73-I29
Federated causal claims SHALL preserve domain boundaries.

R6.73-I30
Cross-domain causality SHALL require explicit evidence of the causal bridge.

R6.73-I31
Uncertainty SHALL be representable as a first-class state.

R6.73-I32
PALACO SHALL NOT convert unknown causality into assumed causality.

R6.73-I33
Beneficial outcome SHALL NOT prove causal legitimacy.

R6.73-I34
Intent SHALL NOT constitute causal proof.

R6.73-I35
Semantic similarity SHALL NOT constitute causal proof.

R6.73-I36
A later state SHALL NOT retroactively establish an earlier causal claim.

R6.73-I37
Causal claims SHALL identify their applicable proof standard.

R6.73-I38
Historical causal claims SHALL remain auditable after correction.

R6.73-I39
No constitutional consequence SHALL be attributed beyond the demonstrated causal chain.

R6.73-I40
No constitutional causality SHALL be claimed where the required causal bridge remains unproven.


