XIV. 🕰️ DEADLINES

A deadline is itself constitutional data.

Therefore:

pub struct ObligationDeadline {
    pub deadline_id: DeadlineId,
    pub obligation_id: ObligationId,
    pub start_reference: TemporalReference,
    pub due_at: Timestamp,
    pub calculation_rule: RuleId,
}

PALACO must prove:

WHEN DID THE CLOCK START?
WHICH RULE DETERMINED THE PERIOD?
WHAT TIMEZONE / TEMPORAL STANDARD APPLIES?
WHEN DOES THE DUTY EXPIRE?

A deadline may never simply appear as an unexplained timestamp.


---

XV. 🚫 CLOCK TIME ≠ DUTY TIME

R6.19 established:

> CLOCK TIME ≠ CONSTITUTIONAL ORDER



R6.74 extends this:

> CLOCK TIME ≠ CONSTITUTIONAL DEADLINE



The deadline must be derived from a defined temporal rule.


