XXVII. 🧠 NO NORMATIVE HALLUCINATION

This is a major boundary for autonomous systems.

An AI may reason:

"This would be the responsible thing to do."

That is normative analysis.

It does not establish:

"This subject is constitutionally obligated to do it."

The latter requires:

constitutional basis
+
trigger
+
derivation proof

Therefore:

NORMATIVE REASONING MUST NOT MASQUERADE AS CONSTITUTIONAL AUTHORITY.


---

XXVIII. ☄️ R6.74 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.74-I01
No constitutional obligation SHALL exist without a provable basis.

