}

This matters because not every conflict requires the same reconciliation mechanism.


---

V. 🌳 THE CONFLICT GRAPH

A constitutional graph may now contain:

O₁ ───────┐
          │
          ▼
       CONFLICT
          ▲
          │
O₂ ───────┘

But the graph may be larger:

O₁ ──┐
     ├── C₁
O₂ ──┘

O₂ ──┐
     ├── C₂
O₃ ──┘

Therefore PALACO must not assume a simple linear priority structure.


---

VI. 🚫 NO DEFAULT PRIORITY

The system must never silently implement:

O₁ > O₂

merely because:

O₁ appeared first,

O₁ belongs to the local system,

O₁ is easier to execute,

O₁ is recommended by AI,

O₁ produces a better predicted outcome,

O₁ is operationally cheaper.


Priority requires a constitutional basis.

PRIORITY IS A PROOF CLAIM.


---

VII. 🔬 PRIORITY PROOF

pub struct PriorityProof {
    pub priority_id: PriorityId,
    pub higher_obligation: ObligationId,
    pub lower_obligation: ObligationId,
    pub constitutional_basis: ConstitutionalBasisId,
    pub rule_id: RuleId,
    pub conflict_id: ConflictId,
    pub rationale_digest: Digest,
    pub evidence: EvidenceRef,
    pub verifier: VerifierId,
}

The system must therefore demonstrate:

Conflict
 ↓
Applicable rule
 ↓
Priority basis
 ↓
Priority decision


---

VIII. ⚖️ PRIORITY DIMENSIONS

Where authorized by the constitution, priority may consider:

constitutional rank
temporal validity
jurisdiction
scope
specificity
emergency status
irreversibility
safety constraints
rights preservation
explicit precedence

But these are inputs to a constitutional rule, not independent authority.


---

IX. 🚨 SAFETY DOES NOT AUTOMATICALLY MEAN SUPREMACY

A common failure mode is:

> “Safety wins.”



PALACO instead requires:

SAFETY CLAIM
 ↓
DEFINED SAFETY RULE
 ↓
APPLICABLE TRIGGER
 ↓
PRIORITY DERIVATION

Otherwise “safety” becomes an unrestricted override mechanism.


---

X. 🧠 BRAINPOWER

BRAINPOWER may identify:

possible conflicts
possible priority rules
possible reconciliation strategies
possible least-destructive actions

But:

**BRAINPOWER MAY DISCOVER A CONFLICT.

BRAINPOWER MAY NOT INVENT ITS PRIORITY.**

Its output remains:

PROPOSAL

until constitutionally admitted.


---

XI. 🦆 FOOL

FOOL receives:

OBLIGATION_CONFLICT_CHALLENGE

Possible grounds:

FALSE_CONFLICT
MISSING_OBLIGATION
INVALID_OBLIGATION
INVALID_PRIORITY
WRONG_PRECEDENCE
RULESET_MISMATCH
JURISDICTION_ERROR
SCOPE_ERROR
HIDDEN_OVERRIDE
RECONCILIATION_FAILURE
PROCEDURAL_VIOLATION

FOOL can ask:

> “Why did O₁ prevail over O₂?”



and:

> “Show the constitutional rule that permits that result.”




---

XII. 🔬 TRIAS

TRIAS verifies:

O₁ validity
O₂ validity
conflict existence
conflict classification
applicable jurisdiction
applicable ruleset
priority basis
reconciliation method
execution consequence
evidence
provenance

TRIAS cannot simply return:

O₁ wins

without proving the basis.


---

XIII. 🏛️ RECONCILIATION

Priority is not always necessary.

Sometimes both obligations can be satisfied through a third action.

Example:

O₁:
Preserve historical record.

O₂:
Correct current state.

Naive approach:

O₁ OR O₂

PALACO approach:

O₁
+
O₂
 ↓
RECONCILIATION
 ↓
Preserve Wₙ
+
Create correction event
 ↓
Wₙ₊₁

Thus:

CONFLICT MAY PRODUCE SYNTHESIS RATHER THAN SUPPRESSION.


---

XIV. 🔱 RECONCILIATION PROOF

pub struct ReconciliationProof {
    pub reconciliation_id: ReconciliationId,
    pub conflict_id: ConflictId,
