XXX. ☄️ R6.75 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

R6.75-I01
Every material obligation conflict SHALL be explicitly detectable.

R6.75-I02
Valid obligations SHALL NOT silently override one another.

R6.75-I03
Conflict SHALL be distinguished from ordinary disagreement.

R6.75-I04
Conflict classification SHALL be explicit.

R6.75-I05
Priority SHALL require a constitutional basis.

R6.75-I06
Priority SHALL NOT be inferred from convenience.

R6.75-I07
Priority SHALL NOT be inferred from execution order alone.

R6.75-I08
Priority SHALL NOT be created by AI recommendation alone.

R6.75-I09
Reconciliation SHALL be preferred where constitutionally possible.

R6.75-I10
Reconciliation SHALL preserve the provenance of participating obligations.

R6.75-I11
A reconciliation strategy SHALL be explicitly represented.

R6.75-I12
Temporal sequencing SHALL be considered where applicable.

R6.75-I13
Partial fulfillment SHALL remain explicitly represented.

R6.75-I14
Deferred obligations SHALL retain their original lineage.

R6.75-I15
Delegated fulfillment SHALL preserve responsibility provenance.

R6.75-I16
Irreconcilable conflicts SHALL NOT be silently resolved.

R6.75-I17
Unresolved conflict SHALL permit blocking or escalation.

R6.75-I18
Deadlock SHALL NOT create implicit authority.

R6.75-I19
Safety claims SHALL require an applicable constitutional basis.

R6.75-I20
Optimization SHALL NOT become an independent source of constitutional authority.

R6.75-I21
BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT autonomously resolve constitutional conflict.

R6.75-I22
BRAINPOWER proposals SHALL remain distinguishable from adjudicated decisions.

R6.75-I23
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge conflict detection.

R6.75-I24
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge priority.

R6.75-I25
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge reconciliation.

R6.75-I26
TRIAS SHALL independently verify conflict resolution.

R6.75-I27
TRIAS SHALL NOT silently repair invalid priority.

R6.75-I28
Every material conflict resolution SHALL be evidence-bound.

R6.75-I29
Conflict resolution SHALL be provenance-bound.

R6.75-I30
Conflict state SHALL be Watermark-bound.

R6.75-I31
Historical conflict records SHALL remain immutable.

R6.75-I32
Corrections SHALL append new conflict history.

R6.75-I33
Federation membership SHALL NOT automatically resolve inter-domain obligation conflict.

R6.75-I34
Cross-domain priority SHALL require explicit constitutional basis.

R6.75-I35
Conflict decisions SHALL be replayable where deterministic.

R6.75-I36
First conflict-resolution divergence SHALL be independently identifiable.

R6.75-I37
Emergency containment SHALL remain distinct from permanent obligation resolution.

R6.75-I38
Autonomous agents SHALL NOT acquire constitutional arbitration authority merely through autonomy.

R6.75-I39
No obligation SHALL be suppressed without a provable constitutional basis.

R6.75-I40
No constitutional obligation conflict SHALL be considered resolved without an auditable resolution chain.


