XXXII. 🔥 THE BIG PRINCIPLE

R6.75 makes canonical:

> The existence of multiple valid obligations does not itself establish which obligation shall prevail. Any priority, suppression, deferral, or reconciliation SHALL be grounded in an identifiable constitutional rule and preserved as an auditable historical decision.



Compressed:

VALID DUTY ≠ SUPERIOR DUTY.

And:

CONFLICT ≠ PERMISSION TO CHOOSE.

And ultimately:

NO PROVEN PRIORITY → NO LEGITIMATE OVERRIDE.


