XXX. ☄️ THE DEEPER PRINCIPLE

R6.76 makes canonical:

> A constitutional decision is not legitimate merely because a decision was reached. Its legitimacy depends upon the authority of the decision-maker, the jurisdiction in which the decision was made, the procedure through which it was reached, the evidence supporting it, and the constitutionally defined conditions under which it becomes final.



Compressed:

NO VALID AUTHORITY → NO VALID DECISION.

NO VALID PROCEDURE → NO VALID FINALITY.

NO FINALITY PROOF → NO CLAIM OF CLOSURE.


---

XXXI. 🔱 THE AMBASSADORS' PLACE IN THE MACHINE

And this is where the Ambassadors become especially powerful.

They create a human/diplomatic layer around constitutional conflict without becoming an unchecked source of constitutional power:

CONSTITUTION
                  │
        ┌─────────┴─────────┐
        │                   │
    EVIDENCE            PERSPECTIVE
        │                   │
      TRIAS             AMBASSADORS
        │                   │
        └─────────┬─────────┘
                  ↓
             CONFLICT
                  ↓
          RECONCILIATION
                  ↓
             FOOL
                  ↓
          ADJUDICATION
                  ↓
             TRIAS
                  ↓
             FINALITY
                  ↓
             WATERMARK

That is a crucial constitutional balance:

**THE AMBASSADORS GIVE THE SYSTEM VOICE.

FOOL GIVES IT DISSENT.
TRIAS GIVES IT VERIFICATION.
THE ADJUDICATOR GIVES IT LAWFUL DECISION.
THE WATERMARK GIVES IT MEMORY.**


---

🔒 R6.76 SEALED

The Proof Machine has now crossed another major boundary.

It can distinguish:

CLAIM
→ Ambassador

CHALLENGE
→ FOOL

ANALYSIS
→ BRAINPOWER

PROOF
→ TRIAS

DECISION
→ Authorized Adjudicator

MEMORY
→ Quay + Watermark

No role needs to impersonate another.

And that is precisely what makes the architecture stronger.

☄️🌱🦆💧⚓🔬🧠🗣️⚖️🔱🏛️❤️

**REPRESENTATION WITHOUT SOVEREIGNTY.

DISSENT WITHOUT VETO.
INTELLIGENCE WITHOUT RULE.
VERIFICATION WITHOUT GOVERNANCE.
AUTHORITY WITHOUT OMNIPOTENCE.
DECISION WITHOUT MEMORY LOSS.**


---

☄️ R6.77 — THE NEXT BOUNDARY

Now one final pressure appears.

Suppose a decision becomes FINAL.

Years later, the constitution itself changes.

The ruleset changes.

The schema changes.

The Citadel evolves.

The agent lineage changes.

Does the old decision remain valid?

That opens:

☄️ R6.77 — CONSTITUTIONAL DECISION SURVIVAL, TEMPORAL VALIDITY & LAW TRANSITION PROTOCOL

OLD CONSTITUTION
       ↓
OLD DECISION
       ↓
FINAL WATERMARK
       ↓
CONSTITUTIONAL CHANGE
       ↓
NEW RULESET
       ↓
TRANSITION ANALYSIS
       ↓
SURVIVAL / EXPIRY / SUPERSESSION
       ↓
NEW WATERMARK

And here ligt een uiterst belangrijke grens:

**A NEW CONSTITUTION MAY CHANGE THE FUTURE.

IT MUST NOT FABRICATE THE PAST.**

☄️🌱🦆💧⚓🔬🧠🔱🏛️❤️

☄️ R6.77 — CONSTITUTIONAL DECISION SURVIVAL, TEMPORAL VALIDITY & LAW TRANSITION PROTOCOL

THE LAW MAY EVOLVE — HISTORY MAY NOT BE REWRITTEN

Status: 🔒 CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD
Parent: R6.76 — Constitutional Adjudication Authority & Decision Finality
Core primitives: DECISION_SURVIVAL · TEMPORAL_VALIDITY · LAW_TRANSITION · SUPERSESSION
Integrated: WATERMARK · QUAY · FOOL · TRIAS · BRAINPOWER · THE AMBASSADORS · LINEAGE

Primary invariant

> A constitutional change SHALL alter the validity conditions of future action only according to an explicit transition rule; it SHALL NOT retroactively fabricate, erase, or silently reinterpret an already-proven historical state.



R6.76 established:

🔱 NO VALID AUTHORITY → NO VALID DECISION.

R6.77 establishes:

💧 NEW LAW DOES NOT ERASE OLD PROOF.


---

I. 🌌 THE PROBLEM OF LEGAL TIME

Consider:

C₁
 ↓
R₁
 ↓
DECISION D₁
 ↓
W₁

Later:

C₂
 ↓
R₂

Now the question:

> Is D₁ still valid?



There is no universal answer.

It depends upon the transition provisions connecting:

C₁ → C₂
R₁ → R₂

Therefore:

TEMPORAL VALIDITY MUST BE PROVEN, NOT ASSUMED.


---

II. 🕰️ THREE DIFFERENT TIMES

R6.77 formally distinguishes:

EVENT TIME

when something occurred,

LEGAL TIME

under which constitution/ruleset it was governed,

and:

REVIEW TIME

when PALACO later evaluates it.

Thus:

2026-08-01
EVENT OCCURS UNDER R₁

2026-09-01
R₂ BECOMES ACTIVE

2026-10-01
EVENT IS AUDITED

The October audit must not apply R₂ retroactively unless R₂ explicitly provides such authority.


---

III. 🔱 TEMPORAL VALIDITY OBJECT

pub struct TemporalValidity {
    pub validity_id: ValidityId,
    pub subject_id: SubjectId,
    pub ruleset_hash: RuleSetHash,
    pub valid_from: Timestamp,
    pub valid_until: Option<Timestamp>,
    pub transition_rule: Option<TransitionRuleId>,
    pub provenance_root: ProvenanceRoot,
    pub watermark_id: WatermarkId,
}

Validity becomes a first-class constitutional property.


---

IV. ⚖️ DECISION SURVIVAL

A finalized decision may have one of several temporal outcomes:

pub enum DecisionSurvival {
    Continuing,
    Transitional,
    Expired,
    Superseded,
    Reopened,
    Invalidated,
    PreservedHistorically,
}

Important:

EXPIRED
≠
ERASED

SUPERSEDED
≠
FALSE

INVALIDATED
≠
NEVER HAPPENED

The historical record remains.


---

V. 💧 THE WATERMARK PROTECTS THE PAST

Suppose:

W₁
 ↓
D₁

was valid under:

C₁ / R₁

and later:

C₂ / R₂

supersedes the old legal regime.

The system does not transform:

D₁

into:

D₂

Instead:

D₁
 ↓
W₁
 ↓
LAW TRANSITION
 ↓
D₁ STATUS = SUPERSEDED
 ↓
W₂

History remains intact.


---

VI. 🚫 NO RETROACTIVE FABRICATION

The following is prohibited:

OLD EVENT
 ↓
NEW RULE
 ↓
PRETEND OLD EVENT OCCURRED UNDER NEW RULE

This is:

RETROACTIVE_PROVENANCE_FABRICATION

Likewise prohibited:

OLD DECISION
 ↓
NEW CONSTITUTION
 ↓
DELETE OLD DECISION

This destroys constitutional memory.


---

VII. 🌳 TRANSITION OBJECT

pub struct ConstitutionalTransition {
    pub transition_id: TransitionId,
    pub predecessor_constitution: ConstitutionId,
    pub successor_constitution: ConstitutionId,
    pub predecessor_ruleset: RuleSetHash,
    pub successor_ruleset: RuleSetHash,
    pub effective_at: Timestamp,
    pub transition_basis: ConstitutionalBasisId,
    pub migration_proof: MigrationProofId,
    pub watermark_id: WatermarkId,
}

A new constitutional generation therefore requires a bridge.

Not a jump.


---

VIII. 🔗 THE LAW TRANSITION CHAIN

C₁
 ↓
R₁
 ↓
W₁
 ↓
TRANSITION PROPOSAL
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
