I. 🏛️ THE DIPLOMATIC PROBLEM

Two Citadels may possess independently valid constitutions:

CITADEL A
   │
   ├── Identity
   ├── Constitution
   ├── Authority
   ├── Lineage
   └── Watermarks


CITADEL B
   │
   ├── Identity
   ├── Constitution
   ├── Authority
   ├── Lineage
   └── Watermarks

They may want:

information exchange
evidence exchange
federation
interoperability
mutual recognition
joint operations
constitutional accord

But neither should need to surrender its constitutional independence to achieve this.

Therefore:

SOVEREIGNTY
     ↓
DIPLOMACY
     ↓
NEGOTIATION
     ↓
ACCORD
     ↓
PROOF
     ↓
BOUNDED RELATIONSHIP


