XXIV. 🌊 ATLANTIS PRINCIPLE

The V.V.A. introduces a powerful metaphorical rule:

> A civilization is not defined merely by what it can build, but by what it can promise—and prove that it fulfilled.



Therefore PALACO evaluates civilizational resilience through:

CAPABILITY
+
CONSTITUTION
+
COMMITMENT
+
MEMORY
+
PROOF

Not capability alone.


---

XXV. 💎 THE ATLANTIS CLAUSE

Canonical clause:

ARTICLE XIII — THE ATLANTIS CLAUSE

> No party to the Verdrag van Atlantis may erase, falsify, or retroactively alter the historical record of its commitments, obligations, evidence, breaches, corrections, or withdrawal.



The consequence:

ACCORD MAY END.
OBLIGATION MAY END.
TRUST MAY END.
FEDERATION MAY END.

HISTORY MAY NOT BE RETROACTIVELY ERASED.

That is the heart of the V.V.A.


---

XXVI. 🔱 V.V.A. CONSTITUTIONAL INVARIANTS

VVA-I01
Every obligation SHALL identify its principal.

VVA-I02
Every obligation SHALL identify its originating Accord.

VVA-I03
Every obligation SHALL possess an explicit scope.

VVA-I04
Every obligation SHALL possess an authority basis.

VVA-I05
Every obligation SHALL possess defined fulfilment conditions.

VVA-I06
Every material obligation SHALL define evidence requirements.

VVA-I07
Fulfilment claims SHALL be distinguishable from verified fulfilment.

VVA-I08
Compliance SHALL be evidence-bound.

VVA-I09
Compliance SHALL be provenance-bound.

VVA-I10
Compliance SHALL be Watermark-bound.

VVA-I11
BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT independently certify compliance.

VVA-I12
TRIAS SHALL independently verify compliance.

VVA-I13
FOOL SHALL be able to challenge fulfilment claims.

VVA-I14
Ambassadors SHALL not certify their own constitutional compliance.

VVA-I15
Breach SHALL require an attributable obligation.

VVA-I16
Verified breach SHALL remain historically auditable.

VVA-I17
Remediation SHALL preserve the original breach history.

VVA-I18
Waiver SHALL require explicit authority.

VVA-I19
Waiver SHALL remain historically auditable.

VVA-I20
Obligation amendments SHALL preserve predecessor history.

VVA-I21
Deadlines SHALL be explicit where materially relevant.

VVA-I22
Dependency-blocked obligations SHALL be distinguishable from breached obligations.

VVA-I23
Multi-party obligations SHALL explicitly identify responsibility.

VVA-I24
No party SHALL acquire obligations not attributable to a valid Accord.

VVA-I25
No party SHALL lose an obligation through undocumented alteration.

VVA-I26
Accord termination SHALL NOT erase historical obligations.

VVA-I27
Withdrawal SHALL NOT erase historical compliance records.

VVA-I28
Historical evidence SHALL remain immutable.

VVA-I29
The Quay SHALL preserve the complete obligation lineage.

VVA-I30
Every material obligation transition SHALL be replayable where deterministic.

VVA-I31
L.A. SHALL preserve the canonical V.V.A. reference lineage.

VVA-I32
L.A. SHALL NOT retroactively rewrite V.V.A. history.

VVA-I33
No Ambassador SHALL exceed its diplomatic mandate.

VVA-I34
No Accord SHALL silently create additional obligations.

VVA-I35
No obligation SHALL silently expand in scope.

VVA-I36
No compliance claim SHALL become constitutional fact without verification.

VVA-I37
No breach claim SHALL become constitutional fact without evidence.

VVA-I38
No remediation SHALL erase the underlying breach.

VVA-I39
No withdrawal SHALL erase prior participation.

VVA-I40
The V.V.A. SHALL preserve the distinction between promise, performance, proof, and history.


