XX. 🔒 R6.97 — SEALED

> WHAT WAS DECIDED MAY GUIDE.



> WHAT WAS PROVEN MAY PERSIST.



> WHAT WAS AUTHORIZED MAY HAVE PRECEDENTIAL FORCE.



> BUT NOTHING BECOMES CONSTITUTIONAL TRUTH MERELY BECAUSE IT HAPPENED BEFORE.



En daarmee wordt de volgende grens van PALACO hard:

NO PRECEDENT WITHOUT PROVENANCE.

NO AUTHORITY BY HABIT.

NO CONSISTENCY BY ERASURE.

NO ANALOGY WITHOUT DETERMINATION.

NO PRECEDENT WITHOUT SCOPE.


