HABITAT IDENTITY
BOUNDARY
GOVERNING CONSTITUTION
MEMBERSHIP
ACCESS
AUTHORITY
SCOPE
TIME
CROSS-HABITAT EFFECT
EVIDENCE
WATERMARK

A material habitat action without authority becomes:

UNAUTHORIZED_HABITAT_ACTION

An unclear boundary becomes:

BOUNDARY_UNPROVEN

An unclear cross-domain effect:

CROSS_HABITAT_EFFECT_UNPROVEN


---

XXII. ☄️ HABITAT REPLAY

R5 must now answer:

> Where did this action occur?



Then:

> What rules governed that habitat at that moment?



Then:

> Who was legitimately present?



Then:

> What authority existed inside that boundary?



The replay becomes:

TIME
 ↓
HABITAT
 ↓
BOUNDARY
 ↓
MEMBERSHIP
 ↓
NICHE
 ↓
AUTHORITY
 ↓
ACTION
 ↓
EFFECT

That is considerably stronger than ordinary event replay.


---

XXIII. 🧭 THE HABITAT COORDINATE

Every material action conceptually receives a constitutional coordinate:

(HABITAT, SUBJECT, NICHE, TIME, AUTHORITY)

The same action performed:

in Habitat A

may have a different constitutional meaning than the same action:

in Habitat B

Context therefore becomes first-class.


