🔒 XIII. HORTUS TAXONOMY INVARIANTS

HTX-I01

A taxon SHALL remain distinct from an individual specimen.

HTX-I02

Classification SHALL NOT imply provenance.

HTX-I03

A material classification SHALL have an evidence basis.

HTX-I04

A determination SHALL identify relevant distinguishing characteristics.

HTX-I05

Candidate generation SHALL remain distinct from determination.

HTX-I06

Reclassification SHALL create a traceable successor state.

HTX-I07

Historical classifications SHALL remain preserved.

HTX-I08

A classification SHALL NOT exceed its evidence.

HTX-I09

Alternative materially relevant classifications SHALL remain challengeable.

HTX-I10

Every material reclassification SHALL be watermarkable.

HTX-I11

Every material transition SHALL be replayable.

HTX-I12

HARUM SHALL NOT acquire authority merely by guiding the user.


