XVI. 🔒 R6.94 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

DEL-I01

Delegation SHALL NOT transfer constitutional sovereignty.

DEL-I02

Every material delegation SHALL identify its originating authority.

DEL-I03

Every material delegation SHALL identify its recipient.

DEL-I04

Every material delegation SHALL possess explicit scope.

DEL-I05

Every material delegation SHALL possess temporal boundaries where applicable.

DEL-I06

Delegated authority SHALL NOT exceed originating authority.

DEL-I07

A delegate SHALL NOT automatically possess authority to sub-delegate.

DEL-I08

BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT independently create delegation authority.

DEL-I09

TRIAS SHALL verify material delegation authority.

DEL-I10

FOOL SHALL be able to challenge delegation lineage.

DEL-I11

Delegation creation SHALL be watermarkable.

DEL-I12

Delegation revocation SHALL be watermarkable.

DEL-I13

Revocation SHALL NOT erase historical authorized actions.

DEL-I14

Expiration SHALL NOT erase historical delegation.

DEL-I15

Historical delegation state SHALL remain replayable.

DEL-I16

An action SHALL be evaluated against the authority state applicable at its execution time.

DEL-I17

Out-of-scope delegation SHALL NOT produce valid constitutional authority.

DEL-I18

Consent SHALL NOT automatically imply delegation.

DEL-I19

Delegation SHALL NOT silently expand across Citadel boundaries.

DEL-I20

Federative delegation SHALL preserve originating and receiving provenance.


