XIX. 🔒 R6.96 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

CON-I01

Multiple valid authorities SHALL NOT automatically imply invalidity.

CON-I02

Authority priority SHALL NOT be inferred without constitutional basis.

CON-I03

Priority SHALL NOT be treated as proof of truth.

CON-I04

Every material conflict SHALL be identifiable and classifiable.

CON-I05

Every conflict SHALL preserve the provenance of competing authorities.

CON-I06

BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT independently resolve constitutional conflicts.

CON-I07

FOOL SHALL be able to challenge claimed priority.

CON-I08

TRIAS SHALL determine governing authority according to constitutional basis.

CON-I09

Federation membership SHALL NOT automatically establish authority supremacy.

CON-I10

Majority agreement SHALL NOT constitute proof of constitutional truth.

CON-I11

Temporal conflicts SHALL be evaluated according to authority state at the relevant time.

CON-I12

Revocation SHALL NOT erase prior conflict history.

CON-I13

Conflict resolution SHALL NOT rewrite historical authority claims.

CON-I14

An unresolved material conflict SHALL NOT silently produce authorization.

CON-I15

Conflict determinations SHALL be watermarkable.

CON-I16

Conflict history SHALL remain replayable.

CON-I17

The narrowest sufficient valid authority MAY govern where constitutionally justified.

CON-I18

A conflict between delegated authorities SHALL preserve the complete delegation lineage of each authority.

CON-I19

Cross-Citadel conflict SHALL preserve both originating and receiving provenance.

CON-I20

A conflict SHALL NEVER be resolved by undocumented assumption.


