XIII. 🌳 CONSTITUTIONAL AMENDMENT

If the gap is genuine:

GAP
 ↓
SAFE CONTAINMENT
 ↓
PROPOSAL
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
FOOL CHALLENGE
 ↓
TRIAS REVIEW
 ↓
GOVERNANCE PROCESS
 ↓
AMENDMENT

The amendment then becomes:

NEW CONSTITUTIONAL STATE

It must not be retroactively treated as though it existed before adoption.


---

XIV. 🕰️ NO RETROACTIVE AUTHORITY

Suppose:

DAY 1
ACTION X

At that time:

NO AUTHORITY

Then:

DAY 3
NEW RULE ADOPTED

The new rule does not automatically transform:

DAY 1 ACTION

into:

DAY 1 AUTHORIZED ACTION

Unless the Constitution explicitly provides a lawful retrospective mechanism—and that mechanism itself must be proven.

Default:

> Future constitutional authority does not rewrite past authority state.



This follows directly from R5 and R6.94–R6.96.


---

XV. 🧬 PRECEDENT ≠ LAW

A previous determination may be highly informative:

PAST CASE
 ↓
PRECEDENT

But:

PRECEDENT
≠
AUTOMATIC AUTHORITY

BRAINPOWER may discover precedent.

FOOL may challenge its applicability.

TRIAS determines whether the constitutional framework recognizes it.

Thus:

HISTORY
→ EVIDENCE

not automatically:

HISTORY
→ AUTHORITY


---

XVI. 🌐 FEDERATION & CONSTITUTIONAL GAPS

A federated gap is particularly dangerous.

Suppose:

CITADEL A → GAP
CITADEL B → INTERPRETATION
CITADEL C → EMERGENCY CLAIM

Federation does not automatically select the majority.

Instead:

FEDERATION
 ↓
COLLECT CLAIMS
 ↓
PRESERVE PROVENANCE
 ↓
COMPARE CONSTITUTIONAL BASIS
 ↓
TRIAS
 ↓
RECONCILIATION

If no governing basis exists:

CONSTITUTIONAL ESCALATION

not:

MAJORITY = TRUTH


