XVIII. 🔒 R6.97 CANONICAL INVARIANTS

GAP-I01

Absence of explicit authority SHALL NOT constitute permission.

GAP-I02

A constitutional gap SHALL be independently identifiable.

GAP-I03

BRAINPOWER SHALL NOT create authority from constitutional silence.

GAP-I04

Interpretation SHALL NOT be represented as amendment.

GAP-I05

Adaptation SHALL require an explicit constitutional basis.

GAP-I06

Emergency authority SHALL require a constitutional basis.

GAP-I07

Emergency conditions SHALL NOT independently create sovereignty.

GAP-I08

Emergency authority SHALL be bounded by scope and temporal conditions.

GAP-I09

Emergency actions SHALL be watermarkable.

GAP-I10

Emergency history SHALL remain immutable and replayable.

GAP-I11

FOOL SHALL be able to challenge a claimed constitutional gap.

GAP-I12

TRIAS SHALL determine whether a gap genuinely exists.

GAP-I13

Precedent SHALL NOT automatically constitute authority.

GAP-I14

Federation consensus SHALL NOT automatically constitute constitutional authority.

GAP-I15

A newly adopted rule SHALL NOT retroactively authorize prior actions unless explicitly and constitutionally permitted.

GAP-I16

Constitutional amendments SHALL produce identifiable new state.

GAP-I17

Temporary emergency mechanisms SHALL NOT silently become permanent authority.

GAP-I18

Unresolved constitutional gaps SHALL NOT silently produce authorization.

GAP-I19

Safe containment MAY occur where constitutionally authorized or operationally necessary, but containment SHALL NOT be represented as newly created sovereignty.

GAP-I20

Every material constitutional-gap determination SHALL remain replayable.


