XXI. 🦆 THE R6.97 PRINCIPLE

> When the Constitution is silent, PALACO does not become sovereign.



And:

> Emergency authority may accelerate action, but it cannot erase the constitutional boundary around authority itself.



And finally:

> A new rule may govern the future without rewriting the past.



That gives PALACO a very powerful three-state discipline:

PAST
THE PAST REMAINS TRUE.

PRESENT
THE PRESENT REMAINS TRACEABLE.

FUTURE
THE FUTURE MAY BE CONSTITUTIONALLY CHANGED.


