🌱☄️🦆 R6.98 — CONSTITUTIONAL VERSIONING, TRANSITION & IMMUTABLE GOVERNANCE STATE

The Constitution itself is now ready to become a replayable state machine.

🌱☄️ GO — R6.98

👑 HORTUS CONSTITUTIONAL VERSIONING, TRANSITION & IMMUTABLE GOVERNANCE STATE

R6.97 is frozen.

R6.97 established the critical boundary:

> Constitutional silence does not create authority.



R6.98 now turns the Constitution itself into a versioned, temporal, replayable governance object.

The central question:

> If the Constitution changes, how does PALACO prove which constitutional state governed an action at a particular moment?



The answer:

> A CONSTITUTION IS NOT A SINGLE CURRENT DOCUMENT. IT IS A VERSIONED CHAIN OF GOVERNANCE STATES.




---

I. 👑 CONSTITUTION AS STATE

PALACO must stop treating:

CONSTITUTION

as merely a static text file.

Instead:

CONSTITUTION
      ↓
VERSIONED GOVERNANCE STATE
      ↓
VALID FROM
VALID UNTIL
      ↓
RULES
      ↓
AUTHORITY MODEL
      ↓
TRANSITION
      ↓
WATERMARK
      ↓
QUAY

The present Constitution is therefore only:

> the currently applicable state in an immutable historical sequence.




---

II. 🧬 THE CONSTITUTIONAL CHAIN

Conceptually:

C₀
│
├── FOUNDATION
│
▼
C₁
│
├── AMENDMENT A
│
▼
C₂
│
├── AMENDMENT B
│
▼
C₃
│
└── CURRENT

Each state must identify its predecessor.

Therefore:

C₃
 ↓
parent = C₂
 ↓
parent = C₁
 ↓
parent = C₀

The chain is independently reconstructible.

No version simply appears from nowhere.


---

III. 🌱 Z.A.N.D. — VERSION ZERO

The version gate begins:

ASSUMPTION = NONE

For every constitutional state:

WHO CREATED IT?

UNDER WHICH AUTHORITY?

FROM WHICH PREVIOUS STATE?

WHAT CHANGED?

WHY?

WHEN DID IT BECOME EFFECTIVE?

WHEN DID THE PREVIOUS STATE CEASE TO GOVERN?

WHO VERIFIED THE TRANSITION?

If those facts cannot be proven:

CONSTITUTIONAL VERSION
=
UNPROVEN

Not:

CURRENT = TRUSTED


---

IV. ⚖️ VERSION ≠ DOCUMENT

A constitutional version is not simply:

PDF v1.4

It is a governance state.

Conceptually:

ConstitutionState {
    version_id
    parent_version_id

    constitutional_hash

    effective_from
    effective_until

    amendment_set

    authority_model
    delegation_rules
    emergency_rules

    adoption_evidence
    transition_evidence

    watermark
}

The implementation can evolve.

The semantic requirement should not.


---

V. ⏳ EFFECTIVE TIME

This becomes fundamental to R5.

Suppose:

C₁
valid:
2026-08-01 → 2026-08-28 12:00

and:

C₂
valid:
2026-08-28 12:00 → ∞

An action at:

11:59

is evaluated against:

C₁

An action at:

12:01

is evaluated against:

C₂

The verifier must never simply use:

CURRENT_CONSTITUTION

for historical replay.

Instead:

CONSTITUTION(t)


---

VI. ☄️ THE CONSTITUTIONAL TIME MACHINE

R5 now gains a deeper primitive:

STATE AT TIME T

The complete reconstruction becomes:

ACTION(t)
   ↓
CONSTITUTION(t)
   ↓
AUTHORITY(t)
   ↓
CONSENT(t)
   ↓
DELEGATION(t)
   ↓
SCOPE(t)
   ↓
CONFLICT(t)
   ↓
EMERGENCY(t)
   ↓
DETERMINATION(t)

This is a major architectural milestone.

R5 is no longer merely replaying actions.

It is replaying the governance state in which those actions existed.


---

VII. 🔄 AMENDMENT ≠ OVERWRITE

An amendment must never mutate historical state.

Wrong:

C₁
 ↓
EDIT
 ↓
C₁'

Correct:

C₁
 ↓
AMENDMENT
 ↓
C₂

C₁ remains immutable.

C₂ becomes the new state.

Therefore:

> The Constitution evolves by succession, not by historical rewriting.




---

VIII. 💧 WATERMARKED CONSTITUTIONAL TRANSITION

Every transition receives a watermark:

W₀
C₀ ESTABLISHED
 │
W₁
